1783650666004499	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4AM		item.comment	bn-1bs	{"body":"Added MESS_SNAPSHOT_LAW_ITERS env override to snapshot_law.rs (default 3000, clear panic on garbage, effective count eprintln'd), documented in the test doc comment. Recorded full-run wall time (3714.59s release, 2026-07-09) + host-contention caveat (~5-13% optimistic under contention, per bn-1l6) in docs/perf/envelope.md Phase 5 section. Verified: MESS_SNAPSHOT_LAW_ITERS=25 green in 16s; default (unset) confirmed 3000 via eprintln without running the full suite; cargo clippy -p mess-store --all-targets clean. Committed 465dc2d0."}	blake3:fyUXy-uEFItvVcKYqNcv-t-wuJDHhZQlKaRtbn1k1LQ
1783650831474410	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4QM		item.comment	bn-28u	{"body":"Fixed: SegmentWriter::resume's boundary guard now returns WriteError::InvalidResume unconditionally (removed the debug_assert! that made it panic in debug and no-op in release). Converted resume_rejects_write_off_past_file_len and resume_rejects_write_off_before_header from #[should_panic] to asserting the typed Err. Checked all resume() callers: mess-store engine.rs already propagates via map_err/?; committer.rs's unreachable!() arm is for append's WriteError match (resume's InvalidResume never reaches it) so untouched; z1_resurface.rs tests use real recovered safe_offset (valid boundary), unaffected. Verified: cargo test -p mess-log green (both debug and --release, including the two fixed tests), cargo clippy -p mess-log --all-targets -D warnings clean, cargo test -p mess-store --skip snapshot_plus_tail green (44 passed, snapshot_law shows '1 filtered out' confirming the skip), cargo clippy -p mess-store --all-targets -D warnings clean. Commit 1a7852d9."}	blake3:Ck13MQvMhcq_VuBL5B1JvCFsN2wxGgRZSUaWQ3_Naj0
1783650909639817	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4gM		item.comment	bn-382	{"body":"Implemented offline archive_reblock(dir, segment_id, policy, resolver) in mess-index/src/sealed/payload.rs. ArchivePolicy is OFF by default (enabled:false; ArchivePolicy::archive() opts in to 2048-event/zstd-19); no automatic invocation anywhere. Re-block reassembles the OLD .pcol (resolving any row dicts), re-encodes at the archive geometry via encode_payload_sidecar (which runs the permanent verify-on-seal = byte-compare of every new block vs the OLD payloads), does an independent second full-reassembly cross-check vs the OLD file, then writes crash-atomically (temp+fsync+rename+dir fsync via the shared driver::write_durable). .pidx is never touched; logical positions unchanged; the one read path handles both 128- and 2048-event geometries (block size is per-block). Archived file carries no dict_id (self-describing). 4 new tests green: byte-exact point+range after reblock, crash-mid-reblock (temp husk ignored, old .pcol serves), policy-off no-op, plus a 1M heavy-corpus bench. Bench: baseline 128/zstd-9 = 30.79 B/event (matches round-4 ref 30.8), archive 2048/zstd-19 = 29.81 B/event (3.2%, ~1.0 B/event tighter; within REPORT H2 +3-8%). mess-index full suite 92 green, clippy -D warnings clean. Did NOT edit docs/perf/envelope.md."}	blake3:l1e27qCoxrndmLq_mAIzzmlEz2hsLdiuSPeOUZl3KYk
1783651560267495	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4wM		item.comment	bn-eyy	{"body":"Built crates/mess-cli (binary 'mess'): doctor, inspect, verify, rebuild-index, retention explain. Follows cli-conventions.md (--format text|pretty|json, hidden --json, exit 0 clean / 3 findings / 2 system). Each command is a pure run(dir,opts)->Report. Read-only ops (doctor/inspect/verify/retention) work on a live-locked store: they report the lock holder pid via StoreLock probe instead of failing, and degrade gracefully when fjall meta is writer-locked. verify reuses mess-log scanner + sealed-body/trailer cross-check + sidecar/pcol CRC; rebuild-index reproduces .pidx byte-for-byte via encode_sidecar (engine's pseudo global-pos offsets); retention explain wraps decide_segment (bn-2ug). Acceptance tests all green: corruption-class detection (log CRC, segment header, .pidx garbage/CRC, .pcol) reusing harness corruptors, .pidx byte-equality, retention deletable+blocked matching the decision function. clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:-hLrEi0hkJMg9eIhgnIP9bRvbTc66gdkGszJTH-EaEQ
1783651743258866	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5AM		item.comment	bn-150	{"body":"Fixed: name persistence (stream_names/type_names) is now co-durable with the covering append. Chose option (a) — frames carry no name payload ($registry not implemented), so recovery can't re-derive names from the log; option (b) is unavailable here. LogEngine::persist_new_names now folds both call sites (stream + type) into ONE MetaStore::persist() (real fsync) whenever either interned something new, dispatched via spawn_blocking so it doesn't stall the tokio executor, strictly before the covering committer append is submitted. Hot path (no new names) makes zero fjall calls. Added mess_index::meta::MetaStore::persist_call_count() (test/diagnostic) to assert this precisely: new-name appends flush exactly once (even when both a stream AND a type are new in the same append), hot-path appends flush zero times. Also fixed engine_append_gate.rs's distinct_streams_overlap test, which used 32 brand-new stream names inside its timed region and was newly sensitive to the (correct) added fsync cost — now primes all stream names before timing so it isolates gate/committer concurrency again. Full mess-store suite green (--skip snapshot_plus_tail), mess-index suite green, clippy clean on both."}	blake3:zwS6AUWfe1sY9QnLnMfwrMnFkmqi319zz0PK-k8ex0E
1783653121352895	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5QM		item.create	bn-3h0	{"description":"From bn-eyy review: verify --full covers chain BYTES transitively via batch CRC but never recomputes the chain linkage, so a CRC-repaired tamper (recompute batch_crc after payload edit — exactly what crash_verify.rs proves the chain catches) passes mess verify silently. Add chain recomputation across batches that carry crypto_chain (reuse fold_chain::recompute_batch/chain_at like certificates::load_verified), a finding kind like fold-chain-break, and an acceptance test that injects the CRC-repaired tamper from crash_verify.rs and asserts verify --full flags it. Doc comments were already corrected to not overclaim (merged with bn-eyy).","kind":"task","size":"s","title":"mess verify --full: explicit fold-chain linkage verification"}	blake3:Cxyw7QjGjcv0ss9tk5iKt6mmZ0Te-3ERTSuK1akOuFo
