1783653671358786	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9wM		item.comment	bn-3h0	{"body":"wave-17 dispatched: workflow wf_e4378cb1-4c1; workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-3h0"}	blake3:PneQgh_uf3TXebzecwQcKOfdn-zG0b_C3Zv5zJLLAWU
1783653862436413	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-AM		item.comment	bn-3nz	{"body":"Root cause confirmed: append_batch assigns the durable global position inside spawn_blocking(append).await, then awaits publish_seq.turn(). Both awaits are cancellation points AFTER the committer has permanently assigned the position. A spawn_blocking task is never cancelled (it runs to completion even if its JoinHandle is dropped), so on cancel the position IS durably committed but the caller's future never reaches the publish/turn step -> the slot is never published and PublishSequencer::turn's strict '== next' wait stalls every higher position forever. Fix: structural prevention -- move the assign->turn->publish sequence entirely inside the single non-cancellable spawn_blocking, and convert PublishSequencer to a blocking Mutex+Condvar so the turn can be taken on the blocking thread. Cancelling the API future can then no longer strand a slot; the events become fully visible (correct, since they are already durable) rather than torn."}	blake3:dqRlKzTd8ojquLtkIUiplgQDZjCcwYtNN_2M9ssyAJg
1783653965732198	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-QM		item.comment	bn-3h0	{"body":"Implemented: verify --full now recomputes the fold chain (spec 05 §3/§6) across accepted chain-enabled batches per segment, grouped by stream, checking genesis on the first batch and exit-head continuity on each subsequent one. Emits fold-chain-break with stream/batch_base_pos/expected/found on divergence; fold-chain-verified on a clean chain-enabled segment. Acceptance test crates/mess-cli/tests/fold_chain_verify.rs mirrors mess-log's crash_verify.rs Case D: CRC-repaired tail-batch tamper passes structural verify (exit 0) but --full exits nonzero with fold-chain-break; clean chained corpus passes --full clean. cargo test -p mess-cli: 12/12 green. clippy -p mess-cli --all-targets -D warnings: clean. Commit cb1d65d3."}	blake3:gwSKYQPNhHj4JAFw4cP8NODaIN8EgCIf0VkIScdCNr8
1783654064434469	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-gM		item.comment	bn-yvi	{"body":"Investigated engine/sealer/cert surface. Plan: generator (#[ignore]) + CI check in crates/mess-cli/tests/golden.rs driving LogEngine (16KiB segments -> real roll+auto-seal producing .pidx/.pcol/finalized trailer + fjall meta name registry); snapshot-with-fold_version via FjallSnapshotBackend nested under the store dir; crypto-chain/load_verified exercised via mess-log certificates::build_cert over the chained stream's committed payloads with hashes pinned in the manifest (engine backend does not itself emit crypto_chain to segments - documenting that). Goldens committed under tests/golden/v3 as store.tar.zst (system zstd+tar, no new crate deps) + expected-events.json manifest; check does full recovery, byte-exact replay, cold sealed reads, snapshot load, load_verified, and mess_cli::verify --full exit 0."}	blake3:TVO24AtPm047JZz-yllN0_32AC7_pwFiZgJlB80POgk
1783654301552984	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-wM		item.comment	bn-yvi	{"body":"Done in 19e4d8eb. Added crates/mess-cli/tests/golden.rs (generator #[ignore] + CI check), committed tests/golden/v3/{store.tar.zst 32KB, expected-events.json} + tests/golden/README.md. Generator drives production LogEngine (16KiB segments) -> 480 events / 8 named streams / 3 auto-sealed segments (.pidx+.pcol+finalized trailer) + fjall name registry + FjallSnapshotBackend snapshot (fold_version). Check: full recovery, byte-exact global replay, cold sealed-tier read, snapshot load w/ fold_version+blob, load_verified green on chained stream with fold-chain hashes frozen in manifest, mess verify --full exit 0. Verified: manifest byte-identical across two generator runs (determinism); test-of-the-test = corrupt a sealed .pcol -> mess verify --full exits 3. clippy -p mess-cli --all-targets -D warnings clean; cargo test -p mess-cli all green."}	blake3:ChE5ggCSwy51juqvXGsNH25gBPf7ARkFIPhSRuNYJg8
1783654837449003	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_AM		item.comment	bn-4pk	{"body":"mess-bench crate landed: in-process ports of durable_bench/fold_chain_bench/recover_bench/sealed_read_paths/payload_replay_bench/engine_envelope/verify_throughput_bench, parameterized by RunSize::Full|Smoke. JSON ledger + floors.json (seeded from envelope.md gate rows + bn-4pk's named floors, -10%/+10% tolerance) + compare mode (nonzero exit on regression). tmpfs refusal via /proc/mounts for durable/recovery workloads. Settle-paced between workloads (documented trade-off vs perf_group_commit's full interleaved-rep methodology). Smoke wired into cargo test -p mess-bench (~0.3s); nightly full run via .github/workflows/envelope-regression.yml. Verified on this host: full run green vs floors (recovery uses R1 parallel path, 0.22s/GiB vs 0.5 floor); clippy -D warnings clean. Commit 6ddc5483."}	blake3:otN3pSpsu0UZ1C8dnrUqCqoGAnychRk0k02k-nk_qIw
1783655530277699	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_QM		item.comment	bn-3nz	{"body":"Fixed (structural prevention). Moved the assign->turn->publish sequence entirely inside the single non-cancellable spawn_blocking task in append_batch: the durable committer assigns the position AND the book/index/meta publish (+ PublishSequencer turn) now happen on the same blocking thread, which always runs to completion even if the API future's JoinHandle is dropped. PublishSequencer converted from tokio::sync::watch to a blocking std Mutex<u64>+Condvar so the turn can be taken on the blocking thread. Also made AppendGate hand out an OwnedMutexGuard that is moved INTO the blocking task, so a cancelled future can no longer release the per-stream gate early and let a concurrent same-stream append double-write a version while the cancelled batch is still publishing. Cancelled appends now become fully visible (correct: already durable), never torn/stranded. New test crates/mess-store/tests/engine_publish_cancel.rs: (1) drop 6 in-flight appends via poll-once-then-drop, prove 40 followers + barrier still publish under a 30s timeout with dense global order and no torn stream; (2) cancel-then-same-stream-retry must conflict, never double-write version 1. Verified both tests FAIL/hang against pre-fix HEAD and pass post-fix. Full mess-store suite green (engine_roll, engine_append_gate incl.), clippy -D warnings clean, snapshot at ITERS=50 / snapshot_plus_tail skipped."}	blake3:iZ24CyOaQf2AoissjHOdv0jJIeThGIYEtOXdSmhTjjg
1783656076110828	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_gM		item.create	bn-3l0	{"description":"bn-yvi review discovery: the composed LogEngine's committer hardcodes crypto_chain:None (committer.rs ~758,969), so the on-disk chain slot built in bn-1d0 (BatchEncoder flag bit0, offset 72) is never populated in production appends — fold-chain verification currently only works over in-memory build_cert constructions. Wire fold_chain::ChainHead through the committer per spec 05 G10 (per-stream heads, chain value materialized per batch), opt-in via engine config (chain-off stays byte-identical). When done: generate golden v4 whose segments carry the real on-disk chain (tests/golden/README.md rule), and mess verify --full chain check (bn-3h0) then exercises real stores.","kind":"task","size":"m","title":"Engine: emit on-disk crypto_chain (wire ChainHead through committer)"}	blake3:PtFMm5Uhjyfpaz9DMlUEGY5A6N2E_3YPd8k4iIZ5I8A
1783656911206150	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_wM		item.create	bn-h8a	{"description":"cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings fails on mess_ecs (unused PhantomData import, non-canonical partial_cmp on Ord type, lifetime elision lints x5). Pre-existing; all session gates were per-crate. Either fix the lints or decide mess_ecs's fate (it is the legacy pre-mess-log implementation — if it is scheduled for deletion per the bn-17h ADR direction, remove it from workspace members instead). Until resolved, workspace-wide clippy cannot be a gate. Note also: the Bash-tool shell does not get mise [env], so CLANG_PATH must be set explicitly for any build that recompiles zstd-sys.","kind":"task","size":"xs","title":"mess_ecs legacy crate fails workspace-wide clippy -D warnings (7 style lints)"}	blake3:CmMsahi8V9f9GpUQWBReAd4nA0kftOUOap8__y8-534
