1783700017654985	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExwwQ		item.create	bn-bxl	{"description":"CI miri (run 29106132079) now reaches the end-of-process leak check (previously masked by the mkdir abort fixed in bn-w32) and reports 297 leaked allocations after all 104 tests PASS. Backtraces point at Arc<Mutex<Option<Waker>>> allocated in SimRuntime::spawn for the group-commit timer task (committer.rs:724 'rt.spawn(async move { rt_sleep.sleep_until(deadline).await })'). Hypothesis: sim tests that end with un-elapsed virtual timers leave the spawned sleep tasks parked in the sim executor, and a waker<->task Arc cycle (or a forgotten executor queue) keeps them alive at process exit. Fix at root cause in crates/mess-log/src/runtime/ sim executor: dropping the SimRuntime/executor must drop all queued/parked tasks and break waker cycles (Weak on one side, or explicit queue drain in Drop). Verify: cargo +nightly miri test -p mess-log --lib passes INCLUDING the leak check (no -Zmiri-ignore-leaks escape hatch); add a targeted regression test (spawn a never-completing sleep on the sim runtime, drop everything, assert no leak — under miri this is implicit via the leak check). All existing suites green, clippy clean.","kind":"bug","labels":["ci"],"size":"s","title":"miri leak check: sim executor leaks parked timer tasks (Arc cycle) — 297 leaks at exit"}	blake3:jEehkxPxAR5xzSja4iEDMq1Ipw3wNZezAz7D7Ac7B3o
1783700024803570	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxAQ		item.move	bn-bxl	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:T_2YgyswDUV2vpp7-4ur6HvbRQ9qM564GNSFDxdoOBY
1783700024819779	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxQQ		item.assign	bn-bxl	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-dev"}	blake3:eshQxXzcnhDEUTIOmVIdMX_jz4NgSoEtY0XK_lqOf-Q
1783700435740468	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxgQ		item.comment	bn-bxl	{"body":"Root-cause diagnosis: strong ref cycle in SimRuntime. Arc<SimCore> -> Exec.tasks (parked futures) -> group-commit timer future 'async move { rt_sleep.sleep_until(deadline).await }' which captures rt_sleep: SimRuntime -> back to Arc<SimCore>. When a commit convoy closes early the timer's SimJoin handle is dropped but the fire-and-forget task stays parked forever in Exec.tasks/Exec.timers; its captured strong Arc<SimCore> keeps SimCore's refcount above 0 even after the test's rt drops, so nothing is ever freed -> 297 leaks at process exit. bn-w32 stopped miri aborting early, exposing this latent leak. Engine (mess-store) uses RealRuntime (OS threads, no cycle) so it is unaffected. Fix: split Runtime-owner from Handle (like tokio Runtime vs Handle). SimRuntime::new/with_fault returns the sole owner; Clone yields non-owning handles (owner:false), so task-captured clones never keep the executor alive. Owner's Drop drains Exec.tasks/timers/ready/woken, breaking the cycle. Verifying with miri next."}	blake3:ESBR5tDRnmng5xMHIIia9Xr42D2BsWxHGXlrVy8PxO4
1783701069767785	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxwQ		item.comment	bn-bxl	{"body":"Fixed in 65b61e0a. Split SimRuntime owner (new/with_fault) from cloned handles; owner Drop calls SimCore::drain to clear tasks/timers/ready/woken, breaking the cycle. VERIFIED: cargo +nightly miri test -p mess-log --lib = 104 passed, 0 failed, NO leak report after summary (leak check passed, ~411s). Non-miri gates green: mess-log --lib 126 passed; mess-store (--skip snapshot_plus_tail) passed; clippy -p mess-log -p mess-store --all-targets -D warnings clean. Doc comments added on SimCore::drain (cycle explanation) and SimRuntime owner/Drop (why the owner is the only viable teardown point). committer.rs timer semantics unchanged; no -Zmiri-ignore-leaks."}	blake3:FWgcePKJBJ8YlnD6mcs4OvjS6zg8jUKvgCSxO92a8Hc
1783701153921872	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExyAQ		item.move	bn-bxl	{"state":"done"}	blake3:KGQCuieoduoQaibiZ7va4yRTIsL_1agQRMZPdrjqwK8
1783701955729560	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExyQQ		item.comment	bn-3hk	{"body":"ACCEPTANCE VERIFIED: (1) all phase goals complete (Phases 0-6 + R done; triage empty); (2) envelope regression suite green in CI at doc-12 floors with documented per-metric -10% tolerance + per-machine floors (run 29106138020 success; workstation ratchet floors.json, CI profile floors-ci.json); (3) crash/torn-write/handoff harnesses green in CI — crash-harness, torn-matrix, sigkill, dst, differential-store, phase3-exit-gate, fuzz, loom, sanitizers all green on schedule, miri green after bn-w32 (real-fs guard) + bn-bxl (sim executor parked-task leak fix), run 29107749696. Trunk aa0e31a0."}	blake3:3oHIDBJSiuBHne3ZxMNvlL7wRU6NAEW-0B75Q_vyGRI
