1783707604505101	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4wQ		item.comment	bn-13l	{"body":"wave S2 dispatched: workflow wf_b4b2e4d9-42d; workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-13l"}	blake3:sp0qk2_ACA0NhHL6NmwCUsU9Vh992Ag_sPbcuVws36E
1783707849687238	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5AQ		item.comment	bn-2xl	{"body":"Investigated read surface: EventStore exposes global reads only via backend().read_global(after,limit) (Backend trait); no store-level subscription/live-tail API at the facade. mess-log subscription.rs (D11 catch-up->live) runs on separate ReadView/Watermark primitives NOT wired to EventStore/Backend. Plan: build Projections<B> as a polling adapter over read_global (catch-up from 0 -> spawned live pump), wait_for via atomic watermark + Notify. Filing the missing store-level subscription API as top openQuestion."}	blake3:KpkaSDV0b-21mje0nBgTFlB_qCmqhDYuNTYgaSt1p08
1783708193683738	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5QQ		item.comment	bn-13l	{"body":"Starting bn-13l web layer. Key dogfood finding up front: the bn-154 ReadModels/WriteOps traits use bare async-fn-in-trait (no Send bound, as their doc notes is 'fine for an example'). axum's Handler requires Send futures, so a generic router over R: ReadModels does NOT compile (Handler<_,_> unsatisfied). To avoid editing the shared contracts.rs (bn-2xl builds against it in parallel), the web layer defines local object-safe, Send-boxed mirror traits (DynRead/DynWrite) impl'd for concrete types (FakeReadModels + a mem/fake writer). Flagging in case bn-154/bn-2xl want to add + Send to the contract traits later."}	blake3:FbCU5O7r-oGa2nTc8c5YV5ia-nphkFzWr_3mjxvc-Xg
1783708303344378	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5gQ		item.comment	bn-2xl	{"body":"DONE @ 7732c377. Delivered examples/social/src/projections.rs (Projections<B: Backend>: home/user/firehose/profile/likes+liked_by, deleted drops from feeds + lookup_post tombstone permalink, rebuildable replay-from-0 -> live pump, wait_for barrier) + tests/projections.rs (11 tests: per-model units, wait_for barrier x2, rebuild==live over 25 seeded random sequences incl. follow-after-post, explicit retroactivity). Gates green: social 56 tests (35 gwt + 8 read_models + 2 roundtrip + 11 new), clippy -D warnings clean, cargo check --workspace green.\n\nDOGFOOD findings: (1) TOP GAP — EventStore exposes NO app-facing subscription/live-tail API; only Backend::read_global(after,limit) via store.backend(). mess-log subscription.rs (D11 catch-up->live) is NOT wired to EventStore/Backend, so an app must hand-roll a polling adapter (poll read_global on a 1ms timer; empty page == caught up) with no commit-notification to await. Proposed store-level API sketch below. (2) No push/notify means wait_for latency is bounded by poll interval, not event arrival. (3) read_global returns StoredRecord with stream_id as an opaque String — projection must string-prefix-match 'user-'/'post-' and Id::from_str the suffix to route events; a typed stream/category discriminator on the record would remove the stringly dispatch. (4) Id is not Ord (only Hash), so timeline sets/indices must be HashSet/HashMap, never BTree."}	blake3:5RT8uTAwjmtThKwVEc4jZFIeNAmD1jtjtzhfba3XzJE
1783709285346363	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5wQ		item.comment	bn-13l	{"body":"Landed in 6b6b5f9. Gates green: cargo test -p social (17 web tests + bn-154's 35 gwt/8 read_models/2 store_roundtrip all pass), clippy --all-targets -D warnings clean, cargo check --workspace green. Verified the running bin end-to-end (register->post->follow->like all show read-your-writes; self-follow/double-like render friendly flashes, never 500).\n\nDOGFOOD FINDINGS (mess rough edges):\n1. ReadModels/WriteOps use bare async-fn-in-trait with NO Send bound. axum's Handler requires Send futures, so a generic router over R: ReadModels does not compile. Worked around WITHOUT editing shared contracts.rs by defining local object-safe Send-boxed mirror traits (DynRead/DynWrite) impl'd per concrete type via a macro. A production contract should add '+ Send' (the contracts doc even predicts this) and delete the shim.\n2. ReadModels offers NO handle->Id resolution, and PostView/ProfileView carry handles but not the author's Id. But WriteOps (follow/unfollow) need Ids, and the acting-user cookie holds an Id that must map back to a handle for the banner. The web layer must maintain a side Directory (handle<->Id). The contracts even ship an unused HandleIndex type acknowledging this gap.\n3. 'is this my post?' (author-only delete button) can only be done by comparing the viewer's handle STRING to PostView.author_handle, since no author Id is exposed.\n4. Post identity round-trips as a String suffix that must be re-parsed to Id in write handlers; fine, but PostView.id being a bare String (not a typed PostId) means a bad path param only fails at parse time, not type time.\n5. Exhausted-retry (WriteError::Conflict) has no dedicated user-facing affordance; handler maps it to a generic 'heavy contention, try again' flash and does NOT retry further (documented in web/error.rs)."}	blake3:tgiNAvnselVH4wNHc3Hapd2ALxq-H-QO_BlqlXLZc-8
1783709819671437	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6AQ		item.move	bn-2xl	{"state":"done"}	blake3:_b9--GgnQvzuDpe0cvFYTqyHFeoXPTylNcp7w1M6e98
