1783718770202655	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExmwU		item.comment	bn-3c6	{"body":"Wave-20 outcome: BLOCKED EXTERNAL. Three independent workers + reviewers (adversarial loop, zero fabrication) converged: ident::Id does not live in mess-core — it comes from the external crate ident = { git = \"https://github.com/bobisme/ident\" } (pinned to 52cfdb6c in Cargo.lock), consumed by mess_db/mess_ecs/examples-social/spikes. Current derives: Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash — no Ord. The orphan rule makes a mess-side impl impossible; a newtype wrapper would infect every API. Correct fix is upstream: derive PartialOrd+Ord on Id in bobisme/ident (one line + a doc note on byte-order semantics), then repin Cargo.lock here. No local checkout of that repo exists and no rite channel is registered for it (the registered identity project is an unrelated OIDC stack) — needs Bob to either clone/patch upstream or authorize an alternative. Workspace destroyed empty; no code merged."}	blake3:ZiDRp46RiIP4iYMjvAEvqDCxvrg24xovOwEfMpt0yIo
1783718775831989	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnAU		item.create	bn-11n	{"description":"During wave-20 trunk verification (2026-07-10, trunk 77d64173), cargo test -p mess-store --test engine_metrics failed 1 of 2 tests when run in sequence right after the 462s differential_model suite (host under full build+test load); two immediate standalone re-runs passed 2/2 in ~2s. Failing test name not captured (summary-only grep). Both tests (metrics_move_under_durable_workload, cache_and_seal_metrics_move_under_workload) assert timing-derived metrics movement, so load sensitivity is plausible. Next occurrence: capture the exact test + assertion, then either widen thresholds, gate on wall-clock sanity, or mark the assertion load-tolerant. Do not paper over: the fsync degradation alarm threshold itself may be the load-sensitive part.","kind":"task","labels":["dx","flaky"],"size":"xs","title":"flaky: engine_metrics fails 1/2 tests under host load (passed twice standalone)"}	blake3:YV0KDajk8yr9QTHZhoMgjkiFq4Xcs2pBVNvTpR2TNQI
