1783724079649430	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvgU		item.create	bn-30q	{"description":"bn-jes dogfood finding: erase_store (bn-188) could not be adopted at social WriteError even though erase_store rustdoc uses that seam as its worked example — WriteError must stay Clone+PartialEq+Eq because programmable fakes (web::tests::FakeWriteOps) return cloned canned Results and handler tests compare error values; BoxedStoreError is none of Clone/PartialEq/Eq. Fix: at minimum update the erase_store doc example to note this boundary; better, offer an Arc-based cloneable erased wrapper (e.g. SharedStoreError(Arc<dyn Error + Send + Sync>)) implementing Clone + Display + source, with PartialEq by Display or by Arc::ptr_eq documented. Evidence: examples/social/src/contracts.rs inline tradeoff comment (post bn-jes).","kind":"task","labels":["dogfood","dx"],"size":"xs","title":"CommandError::erase_store: unusable at seams needing Clone/PartialEq — doc note or cloneable erased wrapper"}	blake3:RwxKFjKiYSp01DWkmgbSG3TCPW5_L1a-HYTB_dMX-wQ
