1783738360849852	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6AU		item.move	bn-1jg	{"state":"done"}	blake3:ewnpYnDsrp5z3bmjLV_9up4l62Dm-e3bwMErBokdWac
1783738361013348	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6QU		item.create	bn-34o	{"description":"From spike bn-1jg (spikes/seed_profile/REPORT.md): every NEW stream forces a co-durable registry name-flush — fjall PersistMode::SyncAll at mess-index/src/meta/mod.rs:456, dispatched via spawn_blocking at mess-store/src/engine.rs:~1775 — costing ~3.4ms and 98.8% of a new-stream command even under Durability::Process. Worse, concurrent new-name persists SERIALIZE on the one shared MetaStore fsync, capping pipelined new-stream throughput at ~1.3x (in-pipeline p50 163ms at k=32). Fix direction: coalesce name-persists into the group-commit window (one SyncAll per batch of new names, not per name) — spike estimates 5-20x on stream-creation-heavy workloads. Durability contract to preserve: a stream name must be durable no later than the events that reference it; batching within the commit window keeps that. Millions of relationship streams = millions of creations, so this taxes the blessed social-at-scale model directly.","kind":"task","labels":["perf"],"size":"m","title":"engine: coalesce registry name-persists into the group-commit window (seed-shape workloads pay a per-new-stream fsync)"}	blake3:0ZNxUEHcgwSc-kxNmQMOKVpjZdszzf97ANuhLcq1JBY
1783738361178753	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6gU		item.create	bn-2cj	{"description":"From spike bn-1jg: the registry name-flush is PersistMode::SyncAll unconditionally, even when the engine runs Durability::Process (which fsyncs nothing else). A name more durable than the events referencing it buys nothing. Gate the barrier on the engine durability mode (Process -> fjall PersistMode::Buffer/page-cache; Group/Os -> keep SyncAll or coalesce per bn group-commit bone) — drops new-stream append toward the measured 0.034ms existing-stream floor for Process-mode workloads (seeders, tests, bulk imports). Complementary to (and simpler than) the coalescing bone; do this one first if sequencing. Contract note: under Process the log itself already accepts post-crash tail loss, so a lost name for a lost-tail stream is consistent.","kind":"task","labels":["perf"],"size":"s","title":"engine: gate the registry name-durability barrier on the engine Durability mode"}	blake3:bhHcknHRzi70EWx4DzaTkLCg7m4QE3hZHuC0nDG08pM
1783787603313933	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6wU		item.comment	bn-3ga	{"body":"maw-dev triaged bn-1m4d 2026-07-10: ALL FIVE items accepted (postsync hook, header syntax, merge JSON, destroy-cwd ordering, ws clean verb); report bone closed done on their side. Follow-on maw work already flowing (bn-ado3, bn-1283 done post-triage). Tracking complete."}	blake3:rCSibiHLNRX2GKmEBbuudX2eOTsBCekkM6XHceefiaU
