1783788667697065	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9AU		item.create	bn-gt5	{"description":"Decision (Bob, 2026-07-11): ditch ident for the examples; Id becomes a newtype over uuid::Uuid (v7), Display/FromStr = 26-char lowercase Crockford base32, no separators/padding. Rationale: uuid derives Ord (dissolves bn-3c6 — time-ordered so Ord is meaningful: BTree indices, deterministic iteration, sorted snapshot arrays all unlock); 74 random bits/ms vs ident 64-bit-total kills same-ms birthday-collision exposure at seeder/social mint rates; ecosystem interop; one less bespoke crate. Base64 rejected: alphabet collides with PAIR_SEP _ and category -, case-sensitive, and not ASCII-order-preserving (hides v7 time order in sorted listings); base32 [0-9a-v] is ASCII-ordered so string sort == byte sort == creation order, 26 chars vs 22. Requirements: (1) Id newtype in examples/social with hand-rolled base32 encode/decode (canonical output lowercase; parse case-insensitively; reject wrong length/alphabet); (2) deterministic constructor from_parts(unix_ms, rng-bytes) so the seeder stays same-seed=>same-store (uuid Builder + explicit v7 timestamp); (3) swap all social call sites incl. typed PostId wrappers and URL parsing in web/; check examples/bank and convert if it uses ident; drop ident from social Cargo.toml (workspace dep stays for retired mess_db/mess_ecs and frozen spikes); (4) tighten + document the stream-name invariant in lib.rs (id now has NO - or _ at all; PAIR_SEP and category routing unaffected); (5) tests: Display/FromStr roundtrip incl. property-style random ids, ordering property (older timestamp sorts before newer, as Ord AND as string), alphabet invariant, wrong-length/invalid-char rejection, full social suite green, demo-seed same-seed determinism preserved; (6) README note: id format change resets stored ids — reseed regenerates. Ord adoption beyond the type itself stays minimal in this bone (e.g. seed HashSet-iteration workaround may simplify) — projection index redesign is future work.","kind":"task","labels":["social","dx"],"size":"s","title":"social: replace ident::Id with UUIDv7 rendered as 26-char lowercase Crockford base32"}	blake3:ubtLO76rm5Tx_ZuLc_5egUoBBoBBJBFwclO-nWxPkls
1783788667813926	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9QU		item.comment	bn-3c6	{"body":"Superseded (Bob decision 2026-07-11): rather than patching bobisme/ident upstream, the examples move to UUIDv7 rendered as lowercase Crockford base32 — uuid::Uuid already implements Ord, dissolving this ask. See the successor bone (social ident->UUIDv7 swap)."}	blake3:so9nFfyVjl9Ko4fz6TNPNca0Y0yNKGHHpCv0BZwC3Y0
