1783789572182232	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_AU		item.create	bn-2rk	{"description":"Verified pre-existing by bn-2cj worker (baseline with changes stashed flaked identically: 0.59x fail then pass; observed 1.94x pass / 1.81x / 1.32x fail): the test asserts concurrent distinct-stream appends are >=2x faster than serial via group-commit fdatasync coalescing, a ratio-of-wall-clocks assertion that collapses under host load. Timed region uses only primed streams (hot path). Fix in the bn-11n/bn-1av style: keep the semantic assertion (coalescing actually shares barriers — count fsyncs rather than compare wall-clocks, if the engine exposes barrier counts; bn-2cj added meta persist counters as precedent) or calibrate/widen with rationale. Do not delete the coverage.","kind":"task","labels":["flaky","dx"],"size":"xs","title":"flaky: engine_append_gate distinct_streams_overlap_under_durable_commit_path — 2x coalescing-speedup threshold flakes under host load"}	blake3:ixMvk-whKJhPbcABXjENDvYEemMlAWm_GGw35TZwOM0
