1783790224246943	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_wU		item.create	bn-3fn	{"description":"Umbrella goal for the Asterism storage-engine spike program (notes/mess-asterism/, reviewed in research/11-review.md v1.1, response in 12-response.md). Prove or kill the design via the research/05 spike sequence A-J plus a baseline lock-in phase. Key kill points: Spike B (composed Process append >=85% of bare log, plus durable-mode gate) kills the architecture; Spike D kills fast recovery; Spike E kills the v4 format. The safest high-value subset (single owner on v3 + resident heads + no Book + effects/checkpoints, Fjall retained for names/snapshots) is valuable even if v4 is rejected. No irreversible v4 work before A-D pass.","kind":"goal","title":"Asterism spike program: prove the log-derived state kernel"}	blake3:mqabkydFwR0O_y9JxvO6RIjD1tfbain4xYOSIRP_Jj4
1783790234536730	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExgAY		item.create	bn-u1k	{"description":"Phase 0 prerequisite (research/05 s2, review C4/S7). Reproduce and record matched bare-log vs composed LogEngine measurements on the same host/device across batch size (1/10/100/1000) x payload (24B/250B/4KiB) x concurrency (1/4 writers), Process and Group durability. The only valid matched pair today is 4x10 (bare 2.038M vs composed 1.710M = ~84%). Do NOT compare unmatched rows (the envelope's 2.96M composed row is 400x5000-event single-stream ~24B — incomparable to the 4x100 bare row). Re-lock after bn-2cj/bn-34o land since they shift the name-barrier baseline. Output: baseline matrix table in the spike REPORT; these numbers anchor Spike B's 85% gate per batch size.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"s","title":"Spike 0: matched baseline lock-in for Asterism gates"}	blake3:6_CeraHHEIkD3ae8vtbRhFoj3qNWjOYM-nt3WzSe4qo
1783790251977824	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExgQY		item.create	bn-hzc	{"description":"research/05 s5. Compare A0 Fjall point table, A1 hashbrown HashMap<u64,Head>, A2 chunked [AtomicU64;2] cells + page seqlock, A3 double-copy cell + selector, (A4 optional AtomicU128). Workloads: 1M/10M dense stream IDs; writer updates 1/100/10k cells per published group; uniform + Zipf readers; pathological one-page updates; page growth under readers. Correctness: Loom model for publication + page growth; randomized readers verify no torn (version, global_position) pairs; bounded retry, no deadlock. Gates: head p50 <=50ns, p99 <=150ns under 1 writer + readers, update apply >=20M cells/s, resident <=20B/allocated stream, bounded p99.9 retries. If no direct design beats Fjall by 5x and HashMap by 2x on latency, keep HashMap and proceed (not a kill point). Deliverable: spikes/state_kernel_dense_heads/ standalone crate + REPORT.md with Measured results vs gates.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"m","title":"Spike A: state_kernel_dense_heads — direct head tables vs Fjall/HashMap"}	blake3:f8geOqG3brBGji-uUMX98yoQ1_qy87gnbwroFPaCVxw
1783790252231467	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExggY		item.create	bn-28g	{"description":"research/05 s6 + review D1. Replace per-stream AppendGate (engine.rs:284-346), per-append spawn_blocking (engine.rs:1777,1844), PublishSequencer (engine.rs:348-440), and post-commit Fjall head write (engine.rs:1921-1932) with: bounded intent ring -> one owner using the existing mess-log committer -> direct/HashMap shadow heads -> completion slots. Do NOT change on-disk format (v3 bytes, temporary Fjall name persistence). Two variants per review D1: B0 one owner inline barrier; B1 pipelined next-group validation/encoding against speculative state (perf_group_commit H2a found naive pipelining a no-win — B1 survives only if it measurably improves matched durable throughput/tails; note B1's nondeterministic barrier cut must enter the fault model). Correctness: same-stream Exact(v) races -> exactly one success; dense global positions; dropped futures -> no gaps, committed appends still publish; conflicts/empty appends preserve API behavior; differential oracle vs current engine; existing crash/torn/SIGKILL harnesses unchanged (mess-log untouched). Gates: composed Process throughput >=85% of bare log on MATCHED workload (from Spike 0); durable Group-mode >= ~95% of current engine Group-mode (review D1 addition); p99 append latency regression <=10%; zero per-append blocking-pool tasks; zero post-commit condvar sequencing; bounded queue memory. THIS IS THE FIRST KILL POINT: <85% => stop or narrow the Asterism architecture.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"xl","title":"Spike B: flat_combined_append — single-owner append/publish on v3 (ARCHITECTURE KILL POINT)"}	blake3:kwclNYvoPmmsi5gyEwYlkboHYImhCCGAgg2tdbieAus
1783790276139031	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExgwY		item.create	bn-2ib	{"description":"research/05 s7 + review V2. Serve the API from log/.pcol blocks with bounded caches; no all-history Book. Steps: active capsule read by EventPtr; block-backed record views; StoredRecord compat adapter; sealed reads via .pcol + pointer sidecar; stop populating Book.payloads/stream_events; remove payload rehydration from open. SCOPE ADDITION (review V2): the seal pipeline consumes the Book — roll-sealer gates on book.payloads.len()>=end (engine.rs:1146-1163) and copies payloads from the Book to build .pcol (engine.rs:1180-1198). Spike C must re-source seal payloads from the rolled raw segment and gate readiness on the canonical published/durable watermark. Seal gate is SEMANTIC not compressed-byte identity: reassembled payloads byte-identical, pointer/version/gp results identical, pack validates + falls back on corruption; byte-identical .pcol only as same-build regression check. Gates: zero old-payload decodes on checkpointed open; peak RSS <=50% of Book baseline on 10M corpus; hot repeated load regression <=10%; replay meets existing gates; fewer append allocations/event.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"l","title":"Spike C: open_without_book — block-native reads, remove the payload mirror"}	blake3:A5YQ3kR6ccktbJoioRclTDyv9ekpUdFf4smUXwpDPlQ
1783790276324552	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExhAY		item.create	bn-23x	{"description":"research/05 s8. Build/compose SegmentEffects, checkpoint them, corrupt them, fall back. Variants: full sequential scan oracle; per-segment effect sequential apply; parallel map + ordered tree reduce; full checkpoint + suffix; incremental dirty-page checkpoint + suffix; corrupt/missing effect and page fallback. Corpus: 100-10M capsules, 1k-1M streams, registry additions, snapshots/checkpoints, dedupe entries, v3 synthetic controls. Inject transition gaps/overlaps, registry conflicts, stale anchors, wrong/missing pages, reordered effects, duplicate application, interrupted GC. Gates: identical state digests on >=100k randomized valid histories; invalid histories rejected or safe fallback; checkpoint open <=10% of full scan; no payload decode for metadata recovery; effect bytes <=16B/touched stream + dedupe/control payloads; incremental checkpoint proportional to dirty pages. Review S3 addition: gate effect-apply RATE so the design.md s18.3 startup budget (1.0s at 100M events) is achievable, not just equivalence. Review C3: production v3 segments have EMPTY extension regions (writer.rs:637-639) — synthetic v3 effects cannot count on a StreamHeadTable; where one exists treat it as partial evidence only.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"l","title":"Spike D: segment_effect — algebraic effects + Merkle-page checkpoint (FAST-RECOVERY KILL POINT)"}	blake3:vRrWGnXSHujW9VJGg2p5-_UmbasorZESLpIrdPwWcls
1783790276528339	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExhQY		item.create	bn-9mw	{"description":"research/05 s9 + research/09 sketch + review C1/D4. Implement v4 header/marker, mandatory batch-ID continuity, frozen control TLV decoder, registration+first-event in one capsule, dedupe key controls, control-only snapshot/checkpoint capsules, v3/v4 segment boundary reader. Exhaustive small-state model (1-3 capsules, 0-2 events, 0-2 controls, sector persistence subsets, stale bytes, crash everywhere) + extend the 24k sector-reorder matrix with control regions and zero-event capsules. Safety: no control/event split; no accepted duplicate/stale batch ID; no gp gap/advance from control-only; registry assignment resolves before same-capsule event decode; recovery stops at first invalid capsule; accepted prefix stable across repeated recovery. A5 framing per review C1: v4 replaces A5 with a safety-preserving nonempty-capsule rule (control_count+event_count>=1), promotes batch_id to recovery-significant. D4 retry tests: (1) recovered-unacked registration+event with matching dedupe key returns original commit; (2) same retry without dedupe key returns expected-version conflict and appends NOTHING. Reuse RegistryState (crates/mess-store/src/registry/) as the replay state machine per review V6/S4 — effect layer dedupes by control identity, feeds each assignment exactly once; do not weaken AlreadyRegistered. Gate: zero violations; control parsing <2% overhead on no-control scan. DO NOT START before A-D pass.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"xl","title":"Spike E: capsule_v4_control_prelude — atomic control+event capsules (FORMAT KILL POINT)"}	blake3:wxofx8swFvlW3fODBThC5R7a4FGWvDkZ-ZOn65aqmEA
1783790306022884	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExhgY		item.create	bn-2gg	{"description":"research/05 s10 + review V3. Compare current ActiveIndex vs microblock arena (linear scan / binary search / periodic skip). Workloads: 1-event and 100-event batches, single hot stream + Zipf, 64 readers, segment roll/reclaim under reader leases. Gates: apply >=1.25x current; head/tail resolve p99 <=0.75x current; memory <=0.7x current; no reader-path lock blocking; Loom/epoch reclamation green. BASELINE CAVEAT (review V3): production reads currently bypass ActiveIndex and serialize on the Book mutex (engine.rs:1640-1652) — the composed comparison must be against what reads actually are after Spike C (block-native), not the component bench alone. If gains are small, retain the current ActiveIndex; it is already solid. Optional — losing this spike kills nothing.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"m","title":"Spike F: active pointer microblocks vs current ActiveIndex (optional)"}	blake3:Ds-os_SmSxdE8YA1VfEGD588NAEvjSr8xmtHsVCfDi8
1783790341003379	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExiQY		item.create	bn-2fp	{"description":"research/05 s12. Candidates: current HashMap, sorted arrays, bitvector+rank, partitioned Elias-Fano, PtrHash + exact key array, cache-line k-PHF packed bins, Ribbon retrieval + exact verification. Datasets: real sealed segments from benchmark workloads (preserve min/max, density, Zipf) + synthetic 30M-key sets. Metrics: hit/miss/streaming latency cold+warm, serialized bytes, resident bytes, open/parse time, build p50/p99, failure/retry, seal wall time, branch/LLC misses. Admission: a representation enters production only if it wins an important size/density region by >=20% with a deterministic fallback; otherwise document the negative result (like D10's FKS decline) and keep HashMap/sorted arrays. Every candidate implements the ExactDirectory trait; MPHF/Ribbon nonmember outputs must be rejected by exact key verification. Optional — losing kills nothing.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"m","title":"Spike H: static directory tournament (optional)"}	blake3:OWSIbAM9BHZaMsxMG1VmMKBFb5we0EglN4U7CgV7sxI
1783790341278849	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExigY		item.create	bn-3of	{"description":"research/05 s13 + review V2 gate framing. Combine .pidx/.filter/.pcol sidecars into one immutable typed-section pack per sealed segment. Inject: missing/corrupt section, wrong segment ID/hash, interrupted temp write, rename without dir sync (simulator), footer-without-pack (fault injection), old reader skipping unknown section kind. Gates: semantic equivalence (reassembled payloads byte-identical, pointer/version/gp results identical); no more install states than current; open syscalls/files reduced materially; seal <=1.10x current; corrupt optional section degrades locally. Install protocol: temp write -> verify vs raw segment -> fdatasync -> rename -> dir sync -> segment footer names pack hash -> publish. Keep parity (.par) separate. SegmentEffect lives in the SealPack (rebuildable); fold anchors stay in the durable extension region (review C3) — never two authoritative copies of one logical field.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"m","title":"Spike I: consolidated SealPack"}	blake3:JMxZ_fiUWdQVaPJdn4L61tWuwCGc4pUwJI3MIO0GyNU
1783790341527489	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExiwY		item.create	bn-2gu	{"description":"research/05 s14. Run all shared corpora under: current composed engine, Asterism v3-compat mode, Asterism v4 capsules, bare-log lower bound. Product gates: append ratio >=85% bare log (matched, per batch size from Spike 0); new-name operation exactly one barrier; head/snapshot latency targets; Book removed with bounded RSS; checkpoint open target (<=10% full scan); dedupe exact with lower write-amp; existing replay/storage gates; all crash/formal suites green. No isolated microbench win can waive a failed composed gate. This is the final go/no-go for retiring Fjall (migration M9).","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"l","title":"Spike J: composed engine without Fjall (FINAL DECISION)"}	blake3:eAexlHRb_iWewOf1jZhAQUcnTyz25z9zH6w763_gZJo
