1783790370546743	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExmAY		item.create	bn-2j5	{"description":"research/05 s11 + review V1/D3/D5. Production dedupe is DORMANT: LogEngine never populates or queries the Fjall dedupe/dedupe_order partitions (per-append CommitGroup carries stream_heads only, engine.rs:1921-1932). The Fjall comparison is therefore a synthetic component baseline built for the tournament — this spike proves a NEW feature (position-span window), not a migration of established semantics; s21.8's 'slower than Fjall by >20%' kill criterion should gate on absolute latency/write-amp targets instead. Compare: synthetic Fjall primary+order tables; hashbrown active + sorted frozen epochs; Swiss active + BinaryFuse frozen; Iceberg-style active; optional k-PHF/Ribbon router. Correctness: exact equality with VecDeque+BTreeMap reference; forced 128-bit fingerprint collisions (zero-bit injection); retries before/at/after boundary; unacked-recovered retry; checkpoint loss rebuild; adversarial keys. Gates: active miss p50 <=100ns; whole-window miss <=80ns or >=5x synthetic Fjall; hit <=300ns warm; zero per-key delete/tombstone writes; resident+disk <=0.5x Fjall footprint. Include review D3's retention invariant (segment with canonical dedupe keys deletable only when end_position <= watermark - W) and D5 batch-level-key API decision in the report.","kind":"task","labels":["spike","asterism"],"parent":"bn-3fn","size":"l","title":"Spike G: epoch_dedupe — exact epoch dedupe (new feature, synthetic baseline)"}	blake3:honiZ5DAY1Ol1qsjy_XryUygeuq4YJivajPpihpR6Eo
