1783796830068860	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrAY		item.comment	bn-2j5	{"body":"Starting Spike G epoch_dedupe: context read (design §13, research/03 §7, research/05 §11, review V1/D3/D5, dormant MetaStore dedupe). Plan: standalone spikes/epoch_dedupe crate with G0 synthetic fjall baseline (position-span adapted), G1 hashbrown+sorted frozen epochs, G2 +BinaryFuse16, G3 iceberg-style bins; exact differential vs VecDeque+BTreeMap reference incl. forced zero-bit fingerprint collisions and rebuild-from-arena; rdtscp quantile benches at W=1M."}	blake3:0teTEkOq98-D9WNPdzqrsXhZqrD3pvWj5F7Ocqgnev8
1783797363753811	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrQY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"Spike C underway. Plan: (1) bench harness (owb_bench example) + baseline capture on unmodified engine (reopen wall, VmHWM, hot-read, replay, allocs/event); (2) additive APIs: AppendOutcome::Acked gains segment_id+offset (real EventPtrs at publish), scanner standalone-batch decode + header peek, ActiveIndex ranged reads, SealedPayloadIndex::reassemble_range; (3) engine rework: Book shrinks to interners+heads, bounded decoded-capsule cache (quick_cache, bytes-weighted) over raw-batch preads, sealed payloads via .pcol reassembly w/ raw fallback, recover header-only + sealed segments skipped via sidecar coverage, roll-sealer re-sources payloads from rolled raw segment gated on published watermark. Key finding already: .pcol carries payload bytes only — StoredRecord.message_type (event_type_id) is NOT in any sealed sidecar, so sealed reads still decode the raw batch once (cached) for type ids; payload bytes come from .pcol. Will document in REPORT."}	blake3:MiqzgQOOA3WanvlcsTOho87o-C_cFt73f9gNSBX_o0Y
1783797818969383	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrgY		item.comment	bn-2j5	{"body":"Correctness gate green: 15/15 differential tests pass (randomized 100k-op runs vs VecDeque+BTreeMap reference for G0-G3, forced zero-bit/8-bit fingerprint collisions, boundary before/at/after, epoch-straddle stale-rejection-by-position, rebuild-from-arena, 0-4KiB keys, scope separation, adversarial 4KiB same-prefix). Found+fixed a real false-negative bug in the G0 synthetic fjall baseline: position-window FIFO eviction can clobber a same-batch re-insert of an expired key (the dormant MetaStore shape only survives this via its capacity>>group slack). Starting bench matrix."}	blake3:SepNCiNmIUiY9BuV8CnKIIRZt_5PVhCXDJ8488BhlvI
1783798444757815	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrwY		item.comment	bn-2j5	{"body":"Bench matrix launched (detached, quiet-guarded). Machine currently contended by a sibling spike's cargo/rustc storm (load ~20-30) plus persistent ambient load (~5); guard holds all measured phases until no compiler procs and load1<6 — will not publish contaminated quantiles. fp path optimized to one-shot xxh3 over a stack buffer (streaming init overhead was material vs the 80-100ns gates); 15/15 differential tests still green."}	blake3:59wK1uiYoR1NzGndAALPK3rw6vZOK0tTmxiBkuDAje0
1783800998035033	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsAY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"Engine rework implemented + committed (4 commits so far in workspace). Differential byte-identity suite green (live/reopen/tiny-cache/no-cache/corrupt-pcol/truncated-pcol/seal_active-straddle). Full mess-store suite green (pre-block-cache state; workspace-wide rerun in flight). Headline (2M ev, 1k streams, same-session interleaved): reopen VmHWM 105MiB vs 421MiB baseline (25%, gate <=50% PASS); open decodes 0 (PASS); hot repeated load 385us vs 758us/load (2x FASTER, PASS); envelope gates all PASS and better than baseline (append 3.07M ev/s vs 2.72M; sealed replay 4.55M vs 3.42M); allocs/event 12.42 vs 13.99 (PASS). Honest cost: fully-COLD fine-batched replay is slower than the in-RAM Book (global 1.8M vs 5.7M ev/s; stream 1.7M vs 3.6M on a 10-ev-batch corpus) — formal envelope replay gate still passes with headroom. Cold random point read 13us vs 0.4us. Two engineering findings: (1) no sealed sidecar stores event-type ids, so sealed reads still decode the raw batch once (cached) for StoredRecord.message_type — payload bytes do come from .pcol; SealPack should carry type ids. (2) quick_cache silently rejects items above per-SHARD hot budget — the sealed global-directory cache must be unsharded or large dirs never cache (was a 30x point-read regression until fixed)."}	blake3:Mc5iMEB29zTdL2BoJWv5r_EdCy1eunZZra98udBqpWM
1783801569417210	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsQY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"10M-corpus results in: reopen VmHWM 303MiB vs 1,872MiB Book baseline (16%, gate PASS), reopen wall 3.9s vs 5.9s, hot loads 425us vs 1078us (2.5x faster). REPORT.md drafted with full before/after tables + verdict PASS. mess-cli rebuild-index updated to emit real byte offsets (was byte-equal to the old pseudo-offset sealer; test rebuild_byte_equal green again). Workspace-wide test suite (no-fail-fast, snapshot_law capped at 25 iters) running to completion now; goldens v3/v4 already green via the locate-by-scan legacy-sidecar fallback."}	blake3:0xI-zz2iKKRaAUtmlg96PZkVSMZZBjGzEVxdlRniu4Q
1783801740915337	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsgY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"DONE — verdict PASS, merge candidate. 6 commits on the workspace (852fcf5f..6c8a6476), REPORT at spikes/open_without_book/REPORT.md. Full workspace suite green: 91 test binaries, 0 failures (snapshot_law capped at 25 iters via MESS_SNAPSHOT_LAW_ITERS; the mess-log early_close timing test passed in the final run too). Gate table: open decodes 0 PASS; reopen RSS 25% (2M) / 16% (10M corpus) of Book baseline PASS; hot repeated load 2x FASTER (gate <=+10%) PASS; envelope gates PASS and improved (append 3.07 vs 2.72 M ev/s, sealed replay 4.55 vs 3.42 M ev/s); allocs/event 12.42 vs 13.99 PASS. Documented non-gated regression: fully-cold fine-batched replay 2-5x slower than the unbounded in-RAM mirror; cold point read 13us vs 0.4us (SealPack phase is the structural fix). API-visible behavior kept identical everywhere the differential oracle covers; one intentional durable-format value change: sealed .pidx offsets are now REAL byte offsets (legacy pseudo-offset sidecars served via identity-checked locate-by-scan fallback; goldens v3/v4 green; mess rebuild-index upgrades them). Reviewer should stare hardest at: read_global's tier-routing loop (active-preferred/sealed-fallback/gap handling), recover's sidecar-trust contiguity conditions + resume fallback, and the seal readiness gate change (published watermark replacing Book length). Do NOT push/merge — awaiting adversarial review."}	blake3:oDh4-wyG8IMfUQI87mlpsGF2tp7ioBuDHIB3SXthJ5M
1783802560944207	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExswY		item.comment	bn-2j5	{"body":"DONE. Verdict: adopt G2 (hashbrown active + sorted frozen epochs + BinaryFuse16 per epoch). Gates: exact-equality HARD gate PASS 15/15 (incl. zero-bit forced collisions, boundary, straddle, rebuild-from-arena); active-miss p50 60ns PASS; window-miss 100-130ns at full 1M window = 12.6x synthetic fjall (PASS via 5x escape; 80ns extreme target met only at <=25% fill); hits: zipf 60-100ns + active 90-250ns PASS, uniform-oldest-epoch 410-510ns exceeds 300 (binary-search cache misses; Eytzinger/k-PHF router is the known fix); zero per-key deletes PASS structurally (0 vs G0's 2.0M on 2M-insert steady run); footprint 0.18x G0 (16B keys) / 0.06x (256B) PASS. Steady insert 4.1M/s vs G0 0.117M/s (35x). G1 (no filter) eliminated: 1.11us window miss, 1.5x. G3 ties G2, kept as fallback for concurrent active table. Bonus finding: faithful MetaStore-shaped G0 had a false-negative bug under position-window eviction (same-batch overwrite clobber) — the dormant code only survives via capacity>>group slack. REPORT.md includes D3 retention invariant (segment.end_position <= watermark - W) and D5 batch-level-key new-API note. Committed 71ba09f8 in workspace; not pushed/merged. (Note: this comment was first posted from inside the workspace by mistake — trunk copy is authoritative.)"}	blake3:PJALmAh_WWH9ZEMv8Gs-DJM5_wKlPlrSwfjO33NwY-c
