1783802672507609	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtQY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike G (bn-2j5) merged at 43e8bd2a. Verdict: ADOPT G2 (hashbrown active + sorted frozen epochs + BinaryFuse16 per epoch). Exact everywhere incl. zero-bit forced collisions; whole-window miss 100-130ns at full W=1M (12.6x synthetic fjall; the extreme 80ns target holds only at <=25% fill — reported as the research/05 s11 anticipated trade); footprint 81.6 B/live key = 0.17-0.18x fjall resident, key-length-independent; steady state 4.1M inserts/s with ZERO per-key deletes vs G0 0.117M/s + 2.0M deletes + 318MB disk traffic. Freeze cost 15ms/125k-key epoch — must run off the append owner. Bonus finding: the differential harness caught a real false-negative bug in the faithful MetaStore-shaped baseline (FIFO order-row clobber on same-batch re-insert of an expired key) — direct evidence for the design's mutable-KV-coupling fragility argument. D3 retention invariant and D5 batch-level-key decision recorded in REPORT s7. G1 eliminated; G3 tied, kept as concurrent-writer fallback shape. Remaining in flight: Spike C adversarial review."}	blake3:gW8t1-93r__s9AfSDKa9Izo42_a8S6C7OI_8RTdjHs0
1783802957668467	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtgY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"Adversarial review verdict: FIX-FIRST. F1 (CONFIRMED, blocking): stale decoded-.pcol cache across re-seals -> reader panic + book-mutex poisoning; reproduced via double seal_active with partial tail block; fix = generation-versioned cache keys + typed error instead of .max(b_lo) clamp + regression test. F2 (strongly rec): recovery trusts .pidx durable before segment fsync without footer check -> watermark past durable hole / sealed reads past durable end; fix = require valid trailer in trust-skip and load_sealed. F3 (strongly rec): legacy pseudo-pointer replay is one full segment scan PER BATCH (quadratic); fix = bulk-cache all batches on first scan + correct REPORT claim. F4-F6 minor (head-vs-index publish order anomaly, non-additive API wording, global_dirs same invalidation gap). What held under attack: read_global tier routing, seal readiness/torn-read soundness, watermark clamps in read_global, pidx-offset consumer audit, cancellation paths. Findings sent to worker; merge blocked until F1 fixed."}	blake3:faIEveO9OfmCAKRA3hdX8iNO94Qya30P-J3H-5rlYmg
1783804248635588	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtwY		item.comment	bn-2ib	{"body":"REVIEW FIXES DONE (commit 08a0d991 on the workspace, stack now 7 commits). F1 (blocking) fixed twice over: SealedStore stamps a monotone install GENERATION per segment; decoded-.pcol-block AND global-dir caches (F6) key by (segment_id, generation); pcol_range additionally cross-checks every cached block against the current sidecar's block entry and returns typed PayloadError::Corrupt (raw-frame fallback) instead of clamping. Reviewer repro now prints 'no repro: reads byte-identical'; regression tests added (reseal_after_growth + roll_reseal_after_seal_active) and VERIFIED to reproduce the exact original underflow panic with both fix halves reverted. F2 fixed: load_sealed installs only footer-cross-checked sidecars (segment_id/base_pos/end_pos vs read_trailer); footerless sidecars (incl. seal_active over the live head) become pending candidates that recover installs only after its scan proves durable coverage — regression test truncates footer+tail under an intact sidecar, surviving prefix reads dense+byte-identical, nothing fabricated. F3 fixed: locate_by_scan bulk-warms all scanned batches under legacy+real keys (quadratic legacy replay -> ~one scan per cache window); REPORT corrected. F4 fixed ride-along (heads update moved after apply_committed). F5: REPORT wording corrected (source-breaking, not additive; non_exhaustive left as lead style call). Re-verified after fixes: mess-store/mess-index/mess-cli 45 test binaries 0 failures, mess-log crash+sigkill harnesses green, perf and envelope gates unchanged-to-better (append 3.39M ev/s, sealed replay 4.85M ev/s, open 106MiB VmHWM, hot 397us). fmt-check clean. Not pushed/merged."}	blake3:M7VPkYRDusKgsVXCP-M-mOJUS66bq88kMRhSTZ6owBI
1783804583236132	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuAY		item.move	bn-2ib	{"state":"done"}	blake3:peefZ0v6LFt0DlVVWALmNlb0c_wmNjCdObbL_q_08cs
1783804600217187	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuQY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike C (bn-2ib) MERGED at f0ab89e9 after adversarial review (FIX-FIRST round -> targeted re-check -> MERGE). Verdict PASS on all gates: zero payload decodes on sealed open (was 2M); peak RSS 16-25% of Book baseline (303MiB vs 1872MiB at 10M events); hot loads 2x FASTER; sealed replay 4.85M ev/s, append 3.39M ev/s, all envelope floors cleared; reopen 5.91->3.91s at 10M. Review round fixed: F1 stale pcol-cache-across-reseal panic (generation-keyed caches + cross-check, repro-proven regression tests), F2 sidecar-durable-before-data recovery trust (footer-verified installs + scan-gated pending candidates), F3 quadratic legacy replay (bulk-warm), F4 head/index publish order. Honest regressions documented: fully-cold fine-batched replay 2-5x slower than the RAM mirror (the O(1)-memory price; SealPack is the structural fix). CARRY-FORWARDS: (1) Spike I: no sealed sidecar stores event_type_id — cold reads decode raw batch once for type ids; SealPack must carry a type-id column. (2) Small bone candidate: refuted pending sidecar candidates re-evaluated every reopen, rolled-but-refuted segments never re-queued for re-seal (pre-existing gap, reviewer info-level). (3) API additions are source-breaking outside workspace (no #[non_exhaustive] convention) — lead style decision pending. Spike D (bn-23x) now unblocked; Spike F (bn-2gg) now unblocked. Next: Spike 0 baseline lock-in on quiet machine."}	blake3:Gz7g_LJiKGcZrMd_Pz_vRLSQV3BhKzOdwvED3NAXhoc
1783804613947864	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExugY		item.move	bn-u1k	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:WQVuF63dLVBHM6ncI5-oxpnq_E3fcmSkkoMhr-JRUbo
1783804613957012	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuwY		item.assign	bn-u1k	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-dev"}	blake3:3255y3sOESc7UP4SOFFtLbvPWvjUG-ocEPdmr3rp36k
1783804665236595	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvAY		item.create	bn-30u	{"description":"Found during bn-2ib adversarial review (info-level, pre-existing shape made more visible by the pending-candidate flow): a footerless/refuted .pidx candidate stays on disk and is re-evaluated (and re-refuted) on every reopen, and nothing re-queues a rolled-but-refuted segment for re-seal — it serves from raw scan forever. Fix: on refutation during recover, either delete/rename the stale sidecar or mark it, and enqueue the segment to the roll-sealer for a fresh seal. See spikes/open_without_book/REPORT.md review section and bn-2ib comments.","kind":"task","labels":["engine"],"size":"s","title":"sealed: re-queue rolled-but-refuted sidecar candidates for re-seal; stop re-evaluating refuted .pidx every reopen"}	blake3:cievm5wmtBHIZWgTVpoklhzGnBFO8IJNIt0DALitYeg
1783804881225013	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvQY		item.comment	bn-u1k	{"body":"Spike 0 (baseline-gen2) START — workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-u1k base commit f0ab89e9 (post bn-2ib Spike C: block-native reads, header-only recovery). Plan: new crate spikes/baseline_matrix (bare Appender-through-committer vs composed LogEngine.append_batch), matched+interleaved ABBA, quiet-guarded (load1<6.0, no rustc/cargo). Matrix: batch {1,10,100,1000} x payload {24B,250B} x writers {1,4} x Durability {Process,Group}, 0% new-name; PLUS a 100%-new-stream name-barrier scenario (Process+Group, 1&4 writers) to re-lock the post bn-34o/bn-2cj baseline vs the old 3.4344 ms/new-stream figure; PLUS reopen wall + peak RSS on a 2M-event corpus via the existing owb_bench example. Building now; measurements only after build completes and host is quiet."}	blake3:EmApdGRHvQbuHEK1cBlCiKbN5Eborh_KJPLfaFmQB7Y
1783805854901329	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvgY		item.comment	bn-u1k	{"body":"Harness built (spikes/baseline_matrix, release, lto=thin). Smoke-checked point runs confirm the mechanism and give an early read on the headline: composed/bare Process 24Bx10x4w ~= 21% (bare 2.67M vs log 0.55M ev/s), consistent with Spike B gen1. NAME-BARRIER already shows the bn-2cj/bn-34o win: 100%-new-stream Process is now ~0.018 ms/new-stream (was 3.4344 ms in seed_profile) and Group coalesces to ~1.05 ms/new-stream at 4 writers (510 fsyncs / 2000 new streams). Full matched+interleaved matrix (batch 1/10/100/1000 x 24B/250B x 1/4 writers x Process/Group) now running under the quiet-guard (load floor 6.0; currently holding at ~6-7 ambient). owb_bench 2M reopen/RSS to follow once the matrix frees the host."}	blake3:MaiJH75CkgDJQdz0GKmbW-SJJ7dxLxQLaRIMQEs7m6g
1783807157739111	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvwY		item.comment	bn-u1k	{"body":"DONE — baseline-gen2 locked (spikes/baseline_matrix, workspace commit a9b066a0, base f0ab89e9). Matched+interleaved ABBA, 3 reps, quiet-guarded. HEADLINES:\n- Process composed/bare (4-writer gate row) rises monotonically with batch: 24B 16.9/22.2/22.4/94.6% and 250B 18.1/30.0/38.4/85.8% at batch 1/10/100/1000. Only batch-1000 clears the old 85%-of-bare line; small batches are fixed-overhead-bound (~15us/append composed vs ~3us bare). Per-batch-size ratios are in the REPORT (review S7).\n- NAME BARRIER re-locked: 100%-new-stream under Process is now 34.4us/new-stream (1w) / 18.6us (4w) vs the old 3.4344ms — a ~100x drop; bn-2cj means Process issues NO per-name fsync. Group coalesces (bn-34o): 4w new-name 1.12ms/new-stream (~1002 barriers/4000 names); Group 1w still ~1 barrier/name at 3.41ms (no concurrency to coalesce).\n- GROUP PARITY: composed == bare (90-103%) at 1 writer AND at batch 100 (matched barrier counts). BUT anomaly at 4 writers + small per-writer batch counts (batch 1/10/1000): composed splits the convoy (~2x barriers, e.g. 1000 vs 526) -> 49-71% of bare. gen1 Spike B reported ~95-107% for these cells, so this is a possible post-merge coalescing regression. Flagged PROVISIONAL; recommend a dedicated 16/32/64-writer Group confirmation before locking those cells as a floor.\n- REOPEN/RSS (2M corpus): 1.67s wall, 105,176 KiB VmHWM, 2,000,000 events verified, 23 sealed segments — matches Spike C's post-Book 104,804 KiB (RSS win held; zero old-payload decodes on open).\nDeliverables: crate + baseline_results.csv + matrix_run.log + newname_run.log + REPORT.md (8 sections incl. how-to-use + gen1 deltas). NOT pushed, NOT merged."}	blake3:-NdIGOb1gMcjDQPlXEYHn6JTQX09PBJeYapbAKfyFII
1783810549606081	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExwAY		item.move	bn-u1k	{"state":"done"}	blake3:yYFpPn8zBSVw248h517sgz2IPJzBC1Q0C9F_W82RohU
1783810571451475	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExwQY		item.create	bn-3pz	{"description":"Found by Spike 0 baseline-gen2 lock-in (spikes/baseline_matrix/REPORT.md, commit base f0ab89e9). At 4 writers with small per-writer batch counts (batch 1/10/1000), the composed engine's committer splits the commit convoy: ~2x barriers vs bare on the same workload (e.g. 1000 vs 526 fsyncs), yielding 49-71% of bare Group throughput. Spike B gen1 (workspace base a3d40ff1, pre bn-34o/bn-2ib) measured ~95-107% parity on the same cells, so this is likely a regression introduced by bn-34o (name-persist coalescing into the group window) or bn-2ib (Spike C publish-path changes) altering group-window close behavior. Batch-100 4w and all 1-writer cells are still at parity (90-103%), so the window-fill path works; the split shows in the low-fill regime. Repro: spikes/baseline_matrix harness, Group cells at 4w. Investigate: bisect bn-34o vs bn-2ib; check early-close conditions (in-flight producer gate / target width) against perf_group_commit H1's convoy-split failure mode. Also run the 16/32/64-writer confirmation Spike 0 recommends before locking Group floors. Cells marked PROVISIONAL in the baseline REPORT until resolved.","kind":"bug","labels":["perf","engine"],"size":"m","title":"engine: Group-mode 4-writer small-batch convoy split — ~2x barriers vs bare (49-71%, was ~95-107% in Spike B gen1)"}	blake3:Jl7KjXkWqnkZaA6afNKALT_h8WLYdqY03G2AVr7PVec
1783810571477151	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExwgY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike 0 (bn-u1k) MERGED — baseline-gen2 locked (spikes/baseline_matrix). Headlines: composed/bare Process at 4w is fixed-overhead-bound — 17-38% for batches 1-100, 94.6%/85.8% at batch 1000; gate per batch size, never one headline (review S7 vindicated). Name barrier: 34.4us/new-stream Process (100x drop from 3.4344ms; bn-2cj+bn-34o confirmed working); Group 1.12ms at 4w via coalescing. Reopen/RSS confirms Spike C held (105MiB VmHWM at 2M events, zero open decodes). FLAGGED: suspected Group-mode 4w small-batch convoy-split regression (~2x barriers, 49-71% of bare where gen1 saw parity) — filed as separate bug bone; those cells PROVISIONAL. 5 of 11 spikes done (0,A,B,C,G). D and F now unblocked; H unblocked by 0."}	blake3:Ksy8FAiYoyJ-i6Q35sz8R8E74YNywHsaS7fAV3YdnkE
