1783810849705179	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxQY		item.comment	bn-23x	{"body":"Spike D start: building spikes/segment_effect in workspace bn-23x — product-algebra SegmentEffect (H/S/P/R/D/A), Merkle-page checkpoint with fault-injected install protocol, 7 recovery variants, 100k-history differential corpus, real-segment head-only integration per review C3, and the review-S3 apply-rate gate."}	blake3:qxjOVl2tKtnvLyVOcuv9ntOQdxJmMQePg7lPDujbH2w
1783812613982219	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxgY		item.comment	bn-23x	{"body":"Correctness green: 20/20 tests pass — 2k-history differential smoke (all 7 variants digest-identical), algebra properties (associativity, identity, codec+CRC, reorder ⊥, duplicate idempotence, constructed HeadPath ⊥), 4 semantic-injection classes rejected everywhere, interrupted checkpoint install/GC at EVERY protocol step safe, stale-anchor/wrong-page/missing-page/torn-manifest fallbacks correct, real-segment integration (production scanner, head-only effects from AcceptedBatch headers, no frames() call) equal to full scan. Starting gate runs: corpus 100k, rate, open 10M, effectbytes, incr."}	blake3:hxDgn0ShHlkqiHbfYZuYjfFIJ71JJE6CDidIg84fRZQ
1783812933637860	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExxwY		item.comment	bn-23x	{"body":"Corpus caught a REAL algebra bug at ~4/100k histories (first run failed, seeds 22280/37499/49999/59902): a ProjectionCheckpoint at position 0 CREATES a frontier entry — digest-visible state change with NO value change — so latest-value dirty tracking never marks the frontier blob dirty and the incremental checkpoint (v5) reuses a stale blob. Design amendment for the pack: the frontier semilattice needs an explicit bottom — genesis position 0 MUST be identified with 'absent' (or entry CREATION must dirty the component). Fixed as bottom=0 in oracle/kernel/builder/apply; all four seeds now digest-equal; 20/20 tests green; 100k corpus re-running."}	blake3:EdrkYdCTRNa-yKb1svG-NlyQcoCwS_KNH8G8mYhcTyo
1783813065541429	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExyAY		item.comment	bn-23x	{"body":"HARD GATE 1 PASS: 100,000/100,000 randomized histories, 74,290,628 capsules — ALL SEVEN recovery variants digest-identical (oracle fold, effect seq apply through codec, parallel build + ordered tree reduce, full checkpoint+suffix, incremental dirty-page checkpoint+suffix, corrupt-effect segment-rescan, corrupt-page/manifest fallback). v6 rescanned exactly 1 segment per history; v7 used an older manifest or fell back to effects 68,692 times, digest always equal. effect-bytes gate PASS (3.29 B/touched stream avg, 4.50 worst vs <=16). incremental proportionality PASS (1.03%/5.01%/10.02% bytes at 1/5/10% dirty pages). rate + open gates queued behind the quiet guard (sibling build storm, load ~55)."}	blake3:4LLekl6XIWTcQ7aMKnNC0iZ2yCovw9zAH47QVhOmz2s
1783816092472411	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExyQY		item.comment	bn-23x	{"body":"FINAL VERDICT: PROCEED — fast-recovery design survives its kill point. All gates PASS: (1) digest equivalence 100,000/100,000 histories, 74.3M capsules, 7 variants [hard]; (2) all injections rejected or safe fallback, incl. crash at EVERY checkpoint install/GC step [hard]; (3) checkpoint open 4.90% of full-scan fold at 10M capsules/1M streams (gate <=10%, and the pure-CPU denominator is conservative); (4) no payload decode — structural, confirmed against real v3 bytes via production scanner (headers only, frames() never called); (5) effect bytes 3.29 B/touched stream avg, 4.50 worst (gate <=16); (6) incremental checkpoint bytes 1.03/5.01/10.02% at 1/5/10% dirty pages; (7) review-S3 rate: 24.31M head-transitions/s single-thread seq compose+apply (gate >=5M, 4.9x), parallel build 6.8x at 8 threads. ONE DESIGN AMENDMENT for the pack (found by the corpus at ~4/100k, missed by every targeted test): frontier semilattice needs an explicit bottom — genesis-position checkpoint must be identified with absent, or entry CREATION must dirty the component; general lesson: in latest-value components, key-creation is digest-visible but value-invisible to dirty tracking. ONE PERF GUIDANCE: parallelize effect BUILD, apply per-effect sequentially into dense state — full ordered tree-composition materializes intermediate maps (7s vs 0.3s at 1t on 38k effects). Committed 1ec935c4 in workspace bn-23x; not pushed, not merged."}	blake3:mZlD4ySrKwXoTLamCtD5NLTLK0DjiAr7Y7EIb6pQiuU
1783816150172976	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExygY		item.move	bn-23x	{"state":"done"}	blake3:JcBrJjMDaU46ZZDt17z-C0sgrIkhHZbTD3oJOpLqoys
1783816168189317	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExywY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike D (bn-23x) MERGED — VERDICT: PROCEED. The fast-recovery design survives its kill point with wide margins: 100k/100k randomized histories (74.3M capsules) digest-identical across all 7 recovery variants incl. corrupt-effect/corrupt-page fallbacks and crash-at-every-step checkpoint install/GC; checkpoint open 4.90% of full scan at 10M capsules/1M streams (gate <=10%); seq apply 24.31M head-transitions/s (gate 5M, review-S3); effect size 3.29 B/touched stream (gate 16B); incremental checkpoint bytes proportional to dirty pages (1.03% at 1%). TWO DESIGN AMENDMENTS for the pack: (1) design s9.4/s10.5 — the frontier semilattice needs an explicit bottom, or entry CREATION must count as dirtying: a ProjectionCheckpoint at position 0 creates a digest-visible entry with no value change, invisible to latest-value dirty tracking (corpus caught it at ~4/100k; stale-blob reuse in incremental checkpoints). General rule: in any latest-value component, key-now-exists is invisible to value-comparison dirty tracking. (2) design s9.8 guidance — parallelize the effect BUILD (6.8x at 8t), apply sequentially into dense state; full ordered tree composition materializes intermediate maps (7.0s vs 0.3s) and should be reserved for when the merged summary is itself the product. Also worth stating in s9.7: allocator components need first/last boundaries so monotonicity survives composition. STATUS: 6/11 done (0,A,B,C,D,G). A-D all passed => per design s19 the in-memory + recovery architecture is proven; v4 format cost (Spike E) is now justified per the pack's own criteria. E and I unblocked; F/H available."}	blake3:MFufbQettrJdh-xyYaj2kB1sqA7ltMF5kld3Ib3hqKg
