1783816521287873	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0AY		item.comment	bn-2gg	{"body":"START Spike F (active_microblocks): read incumbent active.rs + post-C engine read path (stream_entries_from/global_range are the composed targets). Plan: F0=real ActiveIndex path-dep; F1 microblock arena (32-entry PtrMicroblock, delta BatchPtr + escape overflow, release-published counts, dense tail table); F2=+binary search in block; F3=+skip chain/8 blocks; sparse global batch-offset array vs F0 global Vec. Loom model + Arc-generation slab reclamation test + randomized differential vs F0, then rdtscp benches under quiet-guard (staggered vs directory_tournament)."}	blake3:7uH9qX58ESNkPM5NT8QKHYLx20zwsX_ssVRrmuGJ5ME
1783816652199253	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0QY		item.comment	bn-2fp	{"body":"START Spike H (directory_tournament): building spikes/directory_tournament in workspace bn-2fp. Candidates H0 HashMap-as-incumbent (std SipHash, + foldhash variant), H1 sorted+binsearch, H2 bitvector+rank(512/64), H3 partitioned Elias-Fano(256/partition), H4 PtrHash (crates.io, fallback hand-rolled if it fights), H5 cache-line 7-key bins (stretch). Datasets: synthetic dense/sparse/zipf-clustered at 1k..10M(+30M), plus REAL sealed .pidx DIR regions from a Zipf LogEngine store (small segment_size to force rolls). rdtscp + sorted quantiles + quiet-guard (loadavg<6, no compilers, no active_microblocks bench)."}	blake3:67oFkM6R3qGlS5BK3LZexmygqxBif5bi0aSHngGcIfk
1783817936384719	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0gY		item.comment	bn-2fp	{"body":"CORRECTNESS GREEN: 6/6 exactness tests pass (present->exact entry, generated absent->None, iter==source, serialize/open round-trip equality + re-serialize byte-equality, corrupt/truncated bytes->typed error, H5 overflow path, H2 popcount cross-check vs CRC-fixed tamper). Two real findings already: (1) ptr_hash 2.0.1 DefaultPtrHash (REMAP=true) is UNSAFE for nonmember queries — remap table read with get_unchecked, exactness test SIGSEGV'd; switched to FastPtrHash (REMAP=false) + max_index()-sized verify arrays + sentinel. (2) Its FastIntHash (FxHash) fails construction ('after 10 tries') on dense/regular integer ids — exactly our interned-stream-id shape — switched to StrongerIntHash. Both would have to be managed in any production adoption."}	blake3:0cKORH0i5IixnM4t9wTJ7vrRTHP0Mbola0oPHSV8QIw
1783819180752295	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0wY		item.comment	bn-2gg	{"body":"CORRECTNESS GREEN: (1) loom model of the REAL publication functions (shim-swapped atomics + tracked cells, ENTRIES=2, block-boundary cross, 2 readers × 3 search modes) PASS at preemption_bound=3 in 21.5s; (2) randomized differential vs real F0 — head/resolve(f1,f2,f3)/stream_entries_from(both descents)/global seek(stride1 exact, stride8 containment)/watermark clamp incl release-only defensive skip; escapes forced — 5/5 debug + 5/5 release PASS; (3) Arc-generation slab reclamation: canary-on-every-read, no free under held leases, reads through retired-gen lease correct, prompt free on drain, 30-roll churn leak-free — PASS. Benches queued behind quiet-guard (directory_tournament currently mid-run; staggering as briefed)."}	blake3:DjGHq7TeAzm1OeR5KSkmEENKHb6ZPoZ1TDqtNksvMoI
1783821936687073	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1AY		item.comment	bn-2gg	{"body":"Per lead directive: killed the bench process and discarded logs. NOTE: zero measured rows had been produced — the process had been parked at the quiet-guard since launch (526 guard holds logged, output = info header only). Post-mortem also found the binary itself was invalid: the loom 'cargo test --release' had rebuilt target/release with --cfg loom (2-entry blocks), so any numbers would have been garbage regardless. Clean re-run armed: orchestrator waits for pgrep directory_tournament empty AND load1<6 stable 60s, rebuilds the binary clean (env -u RUSTFLAGS), verifies info reports 568B/32-entry blocks, then runs the full suite. Loom builds will use a separate target dir henceforth."}	blake3:tZ1ML4ZYmRmDe0F7VstgvUapn3bdFjEsIaTjm7zCYMI
1783821942510460	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1QY		item.comment	bn-2fp	{"body":"OVERLAP AUDIT (lead's request): no contaminated quantiles exist. The synthetic CSV from the overlapped run contained HEADER ONLY — the per-candidate quiet-guard (which explicitly matches the active_microblo process name) blocked from 21:06 to 22:04 continuously: sibling bench pids (2802626, 2805668, 2806671, ... 2813166) plus a long cargo build were present the whole window, so ZERO measured phases ever ran during the overlap. Nothing to invalidate or re-run. Action taken: discarded the header-only logs, bumped guard max-wait 1h->6h (it would have panicked at 22:06), relaunched the full pass; it is now waiting for 1-min load < 6.0 with no offender processes left. Correctness results unaffected (as noted)."}	blake3:hVzplJ9NXvHMF018lfJ8V3H5ygZhlHad1FiE_Nx4kVg
1783825535412724	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1gY		item.comment	bn-2fp	{"body":"FINAL VERDICT (Spike H, commit d71a956): POSITIVE — H2 bitvector+rank clears the admission rule with margin for the region real sealed segments actually occupy. REAL data (39 engine-written .pidx directories from 2 stores, U/n median 3.89, max 19 for everything but one tail segment): h2 median vs incumbent = +67% batch (4.29 vs 12.59 ns/op), +56% serial (7.78 vs 17.04 ns), +40% cold p50, build 92% faster, open 86% faster, resident -60%. Dense synthetic holds 1k..30M: +59..75% batch, +24..56% serial. Seal budget IMPROVED not regressed (h2 build 4us at real n; 0.66s at 30M vs incumbent 8.5s build/11s open). Deterministic fallback: seal-time U/n test -> keep current HashMap encoding, representation tagged in header (design 12.6). DECLINED D10-style: h3 PEF (loses 2-6x speed everywhere, space edge capped 14% by the 48B entry column), h4 PtrHash (+47% real batch but 2-3x seal build, PHF rebuild on open, and two crate hazards: unsafe nonmember queries in minimal mode, construction failure on dense ids with default hasher), h5 k-bins (never beats even the hasher swap). BONUS: foldhash swap in segment.rs = +53% median real batch for one line — worth a bone regardless. Full tables + method in spikes/directory_tournament/REPORT.md; raw CSVs in logs/. Real stores kept at ~/.cache/mess-bench-scratch/directory_tournament_store{,_big} for reuse."}	blake3:7ejA0FhEDvT3KP8POM9HUg2Yx1PYn8cmGYYbn26kPVE
1783825594276484	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1wY		item.move	bn-2fp	{"state":"done"}	blake3:UYLTU3hHTDJyftWYgtYPQt1MceRRciFKZ0_-brn_l-k
1783825595681034	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx2AY		item.create	bn-dcr	{"description":"Spike H (bn-2fp, spikes/directory_tournament/REPORT.md) measured the sealed directory HashMap<u64, DirEntry> with foldhash at +53% median batch lookup throughput on real segment distributions vs the current default hasher — a one-line dependency/hasher swap in crates/mess-index/src/sealed/segment.rs, independent of whether the bitrank representation (also admitted by Spike H) ships. Free win; do it even if bitrank lands later since HashMap remains the sparse-region fallback.","kind":"task","labels":["perf"],"size":"xs","title":"sealed: swap segment.rs directory HashMap hasher to foldhash — +53% median real-segment batch lookup, one line"}	blake3:XKJ-eti2eatNsN3SiYgYjJjyQUjOb2tIM4eb3yIICQE
1783825595710489	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx2QY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike H (bn-2fp) MERGED — verdict POSITIVE: ADMIT H2 bitvector+rank for the dense region, which is the ONLY region real segments occupy (all 39 engine-written segments dense, U/n median 3.89 — interned sequential ids mean PEF's sparse target shape never materializes). Real-segment medians vs incumbent HashMap: +67% batch / +56% serial lookups, 60 vs 100ns cold p50, build 4.1 vs 45.8us, open 9.4 vs 66.8us; at 30M keys the incumbent pays 8.5s build + 11s open-rebuild vs bitrank 0.66s/0.74s — the incumbent's dominant cost is its own open-time HashMap rebuild, exactly design s12.1's claim. DECLINED D10-style: PEF (loses 2-4x even on its target shapes here), PtrHash (crate 2.0.1 disqualified: get_unchecked remap SIGSEGVs on nonmember queries in default mode + default hasher fails construction on dense ids — documented), k-bins (reconfirms D10: hashing does not beat hashbrown; what wins is not hashing at all). Free win filed as bone: foldhash swap in segment.rs = +53% batch. Design s12.6 chooser: seal-time U/n test, HashMap encoding stays as tagged fallback. 8/11 done pending F."}	blake3:LxSsB0vmDJfsrmRGUCeFDxHZ3Jynt4or62Oy5iYnIb8
1783826260713127	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx2gY		item.comment	bn-2gg	{"body":"Guard self-match fixed per lead: sibling check now matches argv[0] basename equality (not cmdline substring — my own monitor shells were the phantom 'directory_tournament' procs). Binary rebuilt clean (env -u RUSTFLAGS; loom cfg poisoning verified gone — info reports 568B/32-entry blocks). Measured suite launched at load1 4.2; guard holds only on real compilers/load now."}	blake3:4-IzV_Bs_x7NXyOXFoYvlJYa2XbyaT2KtpIiElyZo80
1783826663052391	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx2wY		item.comment	bn-2gg	{"body":"FINAL VERDICT: ADOPT-F3 (microblock arena + linear within-block scan + skip chain/8 + stride-8 sparse global checkpoints). Gates: apply >=1.25x PASS (2.23x worst row, 5.34x best); resolve p99 <=0.75x PASS 7/8 rows (0.0007x-0.42x; single miss = 4-reader zipf resolve 0.82x where both sit on the DRAM tail floor); memory <=0.7x PASS with one boundary row (hot 0.26x, 4M-zipf 0.35x, sparse 1M-zipf 0.705x — 26% block occupancy, fixable with small-first-block); reader fast path lock-free PASS (structural; hot r=64 p99 90-220ns vs F0 282us RwLock herd); Loom+reclamation green [hard] PASS. Extras: global seek 10.9x at 2B/batch vs 40B/batch; slab-free 0.05ms vs 18.9ms. F2 (binary search) REJECTED — slower than linear on 32-entry blocks. Findings for adopting bone: sparse-segment occupancy, offset-delta escapes at 24GB segment spread (17.7%), composed segment-scan for stride-8 global unmeasured (Spike J). Committed 4a1b84a0 in workspace bn-2gg; no push/merge."}	blake3:T9uHHhAxCmL7LnV8pQBjh7ow7bAP41UuJihgo5bYWoA
