1783880684130001	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5QY		item.create	bn-2r8	{"description":"Four non-blocking observations from the bn-9mw adversarial review (all documented in spikes/capsule_v4_prelude/REPORT.md + review transcript): (1) add a v4 SIGKILL harness scenario once a v4 committer exists (deferred in Spike E because v4 write is off by default and no committer path exists); (2) the v3-only-binary refuses-v4-directory rule is by-construction (directory_contains_v4_segment/peek_segment_format tested) but the open-time refusal must be wired+tested when building any v3-only binary; (3) marker_flags/marker_reserved are CRC-covered but not checked ==0 on read — forward-compat asymmetry, add mask checks; (4) add a direct validate_capsule-vs-decode_capsule acceptance-differential fuzz target (currently equivalent by construction, cheap to pin).","kind":"task","labels":["engine","asterism"],"size":"s","title":"v4 follow-ups from Spike E review: SIGKILL scenario when v4 committer lands; v3-binary open-time refusal; marker_flags==0 read check; validate-vs-decode differential fuzz"}	blake3:2_ebg1BdVYgG6cVzIgasqRQdldDV-t1FQvxpOVd4n_4
