1783880684180169	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx5wY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike E (bn-9mw) MERGED after adversarial review (verdict MERGE, zero blocking findings — reviewer traced CRC coverage byte-for-byte, defeated stale-epoch/batch-id attacks, confirmed the exhaustive model drives the REAL scanner and D4 reaches real RegistryState). FORMAT KILL POINT CLEARED: 96,654 exhaustive crash-model states + 24,000 torn-matrix cases + 30M fuzz execs, zero safety violations; v3 suites untouched-green; scan overhead +0.47%/byte via the validate/materialize split (naive decode was +24.5% — MANDATORY design amendment: the normative v4 spec must specify the no-alloc validate fast path). All research/09 s23 open decisions resolved and documented (header_crc dropped, 32B marker, all controls critical, UTF-8-only). v4 write remains OFF by default — no store writes v4 until migration. Follow-ups boned separately. 10/11 done. Spike I (SealPack) still in flight; J unblocks when I lands."}	blake3:KEqFU1uE6zaUwbUXPwIObXQqpoDODp1hulGmFQdrHjM
1783885625159740	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6AY		item.create	bn-11g	{"description":"Deferred from bn-3of review F2 with explicit lead sign-off: the segment footer currently trusts a .seal on coverage match (segment_id/base_pos/end_pos) alone — it does not name the pack hash, deviating from research/04 s6.1/6.2's 'footer binds pack identity'. Reviewer assessed correctness impact negligible under the real system (one .seal per segment_id, atomic rename, blake3 catches bitrot), so coverage-only trust is ACCEPTED for the default-OFF flag period. Before seal_pack becomes default: bind the pack identity (post-F1-fix: the header+directory hash, since the directory commits to per-section CRCs/content-hash prefixes) into the trailer extension region (spec 01 s3.3.2, currently Phase-3 empty), and validate it in load_sealed install. See spikes/seal_pack/REPORT.md and bn-3of review comments.","kind":"task","labels":["engine","asterism"],"size":"s","title":"SealPack: bind pack identity into the segment footer (research/04 s6.2 trust chain)"}	blake3:Y0SzH41zF4ZEi7Fs0ODXbGQgdMuX0SXxtN7iaoqV6Xc
1783885625200076	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6QY		item.comment	bn-3of	{"body":"Adversarial review verdict: FIX-FIRST (no correctness blocker; every corruption path degrades to safe raw scan; byte-identity proven). Lead decisions: F1 -> fix with option (b) variant: whole-pack hash restricted to header+directory (directory transitively commits section contents via per-section crc32c + content_hash_prefix), so a bit-flipped OPTIONAL section fails its own CRC and drops locally while the rest of the pack keeps serving — restores the designed degradation AND preserves identity binding; rewrite the degradation test to flip a real byte with NO trailer-hash repair. F2 -> ACCEPTED for the default-OFF period (coverage-only footer trust), follow-up bone filed for footer identity binding via trailer extension region before flag-default-ON. F3 -> discharge-by-construction ACCEPTED; REPORT must document the actual verification chain honestly (not claim s11.3 step 2 verbatim) + add a cheap EVENT_TYPE_IDS section decode round-trip self-check before write. Plus: full cargo test -p mess-index -p mess-store --release must complete on the quiet machine before merge (reviewer's run jammed on a shared build lock)."}	blake3:70JXF_ihD_laBvcFFEsuMVXSH0aH6gK0dNLg-K2ze7A
1783897897455659	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6gY		item.move	bn-3of	{"state":"done"}	blake3:NwjgyD45ABFTq2hKnJrIMucMoudZNPlohGVW--OkMEg
1783897931625579	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6wY		item.comment	bn-3fn	{"body":"Spike I (bn-3of) MERGED at 81502c0c after adversarial review (FIX-FIRST -> fixes verified by lead -> full suite green, 30 test binaries 0 failures). Verdict ADMIT (behind EngineOptions::seal_pack, default OFF). Gates: install states 3 renames -> 1; sealed-tier file opens on reopen 153 -> 51 (-66.7%); seal wall 1.04x; cold read p99 45.2us -> 39.7us (IMPROVES — the new EVENT_TYPE_IDS column lets decode_capsule skip raw-frame decode entirely, closing the Spike C carry-forward that no sidecar stored event_type_id); byte-identical replay proven by differential. EVENT_TYPE_IDS design: distinct-type dictionary + adaptive-width per-event indices (1B for <=256 types) ~= 1B/event. Review findings resolved: F1 (REAL fix, format changed pre-ship) — pack hash narrowed to header+directory [0,sections_off) so a bit-flip in an OPTIONAL section fails only its own directory-committed CRC and drops locally, instead of the whole-bytes hash rejecting the entire pack and forcing a full raw scan; mandatory sections must still be present AND crc-valid or the pack is refused; the old degradation test was bogus (it repaired the trailer hash after corrupting a byte) and now flips a real byte with no repair. F2 (footer does not name pack hash, deviating from research/04 s6.2) ACCEPTED for the default-OFF period — bone bn-11g must land before seal_pack defaults ON. F3 verify_pack stays pointer-only (payload bytes already byte-verified by verify-on-seal) + added EVENT_TYPE_IDS decode-back self-check at seal. ALL 11 SPIKES DONE. Spike J (bn-2gu) is the only remaining item — the final composed go/no-go."}	blake3:3fdjnaTwPLuN3pY8eP5a5Kw6BgDs4vW61kdtw1poEgs
