1784041718204804	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExmwk		item.update	bn-k8qd	{"field":"title","value":"Freeze snapshot choice and conditional control constraints"}	blake3:2YJarewC-HMqbAA331myvyTpScaYRkIne2-gZ_lMFS8
1784041718214668	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnAk		item.update	bn-k8qd	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nThe landed authority audit disproved the premise that snapshot installs, projection checkpoints, and dedupe keys must all become log controls before Fjall can be removed. Snapshot discovery is live but discardable: losing its Fjall head causes a correct full replay. Projection checkpoint and dedupe MetaStore APIs have no production callers. Canonical controls remain possible product choices, not deletion prerequisites.\n\n# Goal\nProduce one bounded ADR that chooses the replacement authority/publication semantics for snapshot discovery and freezes the cross-cutting constraints for any later admitted projection-checkpoint or exact-dedupe control. Classify the latter capabilities as optional and route their final product ADMIT/DECLINE decisions to bn-11mk and bn-2ctq rather than duplicating those gates. Declined capabilities must have an explicit API-removal or demotion path.\n\n# Decision Inputs\nCompare authority, publication order, crash fallback, global-position semantics, retry behavior, recovery cost, allocation-free validation, retention, compatibility, downgrade refusal, and operational observability. Preserve discardable semantics where they satisfy the contract; never promote an accelerator to authority by default.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A capability table classifies snapshot discovery, projection checkpoints, exact dedupe, and registry separately as canonical, discardable/rebuildable, dormant, required, or optional.\n- [ ] Snapshot discovery chooses either a self-describing pack plus discardable discovery metadata or a canonical install transition, with crash-before/after-publication behavior and full-replay fallback specified.\n- [ ] Projection checkpoints are explicitly routed to bn-11mk for ADMIT/DECLINE and exact batch idempotency to bn-2ctq; this ADR states the authority/encoding constraints each admitted branch must satisfy without pre-empting its user-value decision.\n- [ ] Every canonical v3 control states identity, retry, retention, recovery, and its effect on visible global-position gaps and opaque cursors.\n- [ ] Pulling v4 forward is allowed only by an explicit ADR amendment that rewires or closes redundant Phase 9 work.\n- [ ] Downstream bones and dependencies are updated to match the classifications; no dormant capability remains a Fjall-deletion blocker.\n- [ ] Adversarial review covers torn writes, barriers, corrupt discovery state, duplicates, downgrade refusal, and recovery from canonical bytes.\n\n# Project Value\nSeparates required snapshot integration from optional product features and gives every later decision/implementation bone one non-contradictory authority envelope."}	blake3:LtDZC1BI698XPqGH0Os5LJNdvt_GaDBHnz_6QPIypE0
1784041718230852	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnQk		item.comment	bn-k8qd	{"body":"Grooming correction: final projection ADMIT/DECLINE remains owned by bn-11mk and exact batch-idempotency by bn-2ctq. This ADR chooses snapshot semantics and freezes shared authority/encoding constraints without duplicating those product gates."}	blake3:TKf3pmtk8W1JoNCmfdlcrnPzUwt5kf2P92yV1Tea7qg
1784041793611225	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExngk		item.update	bn-ogn	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nThe post-spike design pack contained stale authority claims. The landed source-traced audit now shows that LogEngine is already independent of MetaStore, FjallSnapshotBackend is the only live production Fjall consumer, snapshot discovery is discardable acceleration state, and MetaStore projection checkpoints and dedupe are dormant. There are no stores or users to migrate.\n\n# Goal\nFreeze the remaining implementation contract against current code and accepted measurements. Resolve documentation contradictions, record the no-migration scope, define opaque global-cursor semantics, choose snapshot-discovery semantics, and freeze the authority envelope for optional projection-checkpoint and dedupe controls without inventing them merely to justify Fjall deletion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Current code ownership and every Fjall keyspace/API are classified as canonical authority, rebuildable/discardable acceleration, dormant compatibility surface, or removable.\n- A reviewed ADR chooses the snapshot-discovery replacement, classifies projection checkpoints and exact dedupe as optional, and routes their final product decisions to bn-11mk and bn-2ctq.\n- Any later-admitted canonical log transition states its global-position, retry, durability, recovery, and downgrade consequences; v4 remains a separate explicit product decision unless the graph is deliberately rewired.\n- State frontiers, fairness/cancellation, retention, and batch-stratified performance contracts are explicit.\n- Design and research manifests identify amendments and historical documents unambiguously.\n\n# Why\nThis prevents building replacements for dormant APIs, making accelerators authoritative, duplicating product-decision gates, or treating a component implementation as completed Fjall integration.\n\n# Exit Gate\nClose manually only after all five children are done, the authority audit and capability ADR have adversarial review, the design/research amendments cross-reference the chosen contracts, and all dependency changes pass triage validation with zero scheduling violations."}	blake3:sTC4AipiZx6LKESuG7wb12OhzsdrJ75syKU7Dx-XDzA
1784041803645608	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExnwk		item.comment	bn-25c	{"body":"Independent review changes requested: unsafe Subscription::position persistence after next() prefetch, missing app-facing CursorRegressed integration, exclusive-watermark off-by-one, unchecked u64::MAX cursor arithmetic, and overstrong cancellation wording. Worker is addressing all before merge; targeted pre-fix subscription/doc tests otherwise passed."}	blake3:biau8USvFO819h2QLeYdHTg60hPX4FSDHXeojX__vpg
1784041953590279	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwAQ		item.link	bn-2ctq	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-k8qd"}	blake3:NQcmQgpWs072DObvHwPtpziwq4VfIhMIU8C31MmhqAM
1784041953616715	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwAg		item.comment	bn-11mk	{"body":"ADR 0002 routes the final projection ADMIT/DECLINE here. ADMIT must satisfy bounded canonical identity, authorization, retry/rewind, retention, raw-log recovery, explicit presence-at-zero, allocation-free validation, opaque-cursor/global-gap semantics, observability, and production-consumer A/B evidence. DECLINE removes/demotes the dormant API. Existing dependencies are unchanged; this remains independent of Fjall deletion."}	blake3:Io0TPGBVmndzdTwA-vc1n6pi6NzL17NnND-2SLjydUE
1784041953639357	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwAw		item.comment	bn-1ojm	{"body":"ADR 0002 does not pull v4 forward. Snapshot discovery uses a discardable sidecar. Any optional projection/idempotency ADMIT branch that requires v4 must amend ADR 0002 and rewire redundant Phase 9 work through this gate; unknown canonical versions remain fail-closed."}	blake3:aML1N0MFHrOwdDw7G1ujC9Z0c1HlJjx5f7SDTdu9rIk
1784041953653376	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwBA		item.comment	bn-2hkp	{"body":"ADR 0002 is the normative capability overlay for pack reconciliation: snapshot packs plus discardable discovery are selected; projection checkpoints and exact batch idempotency remain optional under bn-11mk/bn-2ctq; v4 remains separate. Preserve the conditional encoding/global-cursor constraints when updating the broader design pack."}	blake3:yS8Nrn8iTF5VNkHBnk0lEjGjXqQeICtE-b8cpjj8YNA
1784041953664936	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwBQ		item.update	bn-ozi5	{"field":"description","value":"Context: The authority audit proved that Fjall snapshot heads are discardable acceleration state, not event authority. ADR 0002 selects immutable self-describing snapshot packs plus generation-stamped discardable discovery metadata. No SnapshotInstalled log control is admitted; loss or corruption must fall back to canonical event replay.\n\nGoal: Replace FjallSnapshotBackend discovery with the selected pack and manifest protocol. Implement bounded immutable records, validated pack/footer framing, pack-before-manifest durability, monotone concurrent publication, orphan collection inputs, safe fallback, and storage-neutral backend/offline-reader integration hooks.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- Pack records are self-describing, bounded, hash-verified, and durable before discovery publication.\n- Optional state and event-prefix hashes have explicit presence encodings.\n- Discovery manifests are generation-stamped and atomic but discardable; missing, torn, stale, unknown, or corrupt state selects older validated state or full replay.\n- Lower-version concurrent saves cannot regress the head; identical same-version saves are idempotent; conflicting same-version identities are diagnosed and retain the current head.\n- No published entry names missing or unverified bytes; orphan packs are safe and collectable only from a durable reachability view.\n- Snapshot state never authorizes event retention and every former Fjall corruption class remains availability-safe.\n- The replacement exposes application and offline-tool integration hooks and has no Fjall dependency.\n- Interleaved A/B compares Fjall and replacement through public EventStore callers: save/load hit and forced fallback p50/p99, reopen, file count, bytes/write amplification, peak RSS, and events replayed. Raw rows and environment/load metadata are committed.\n- The flat-owner 32-cell matrix shows zero material cost when snapshot policy is off.\n\nProject Value: Removes the only live Fjall role while preserving the smallest correct discardable-acceleration contract."}	blake3:t2Wh5ABkBEeB17WUhAQxPKqVGnjczOpuCsjG-GbYghc
1784041953684297	mess-control-adr	itc:v3:AWKZM-ZOc5kyZEAAAAAAQbW-13drWgAAAAEwBg		item.comment	bn-2ctq	{"body":"ADR 0002 routes the final exact batch-idempotency ADMIT/DECLINE here and now blocks this decision. ADMIT must freeze bounded scope/key/authorization, original-result retry semantics, atomic key+event encoding, exact retention, allocation-free recovery validation, public owner/recovery A/B, and v3-gap or v4 consequences. Two ordered v3 batches are not atomic enough. DECLINE closes downstream implementation and removes dead Fjall/options."}	blake3:rRDFZpXEbdPTY9T9uUVE9x92STUri845T2e1qz4qEls
1784041995162244	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoAk		item.update	bn-11mk	{"field":"title","value":"Decide whether engine-owned projection checkpoints earn a product contract"}	blake3:MQ5YBXTyhX_9yQsv2cKDBO34_vC28G6KqOqfE_exVDE
1784041995170940	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoQk		item.update	bn-11mk	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nMetaStore exposes projection checkpoint positions, but the authority audit found no production caller. The real social projection uses a versioned, discardable application-owned sidecar. Engine-owned projection checkpoints are therefore an optional product capability, not state that must be migrated and not a Fjall-deletion blocker. This decision must happen before building dense projection slots.\n\n# Goal\nMake a bounded ADMIT or DECLINE decision for engine-owned projection checkpoints. If ADMIT, freeze the public contract and create/rewrite the downstream component and Phase 7 integration work. If DECLINE, close the conditional dense-slot work, remove or demote dormant MetaStore APIs during cleanup, and retain the documented application-owned sidecar pattern.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Decision states the concrete user/job value, adopted caller, authorization model, and why engine ownership is preferable to application-owned discardable state.\n- [ ] ADMIT: projector identity, opaque frontier, optional digest, monotonicity/rewind policy, retention, global-position behavior, and public API are normative.\n- [ ] ADMIT: publication follows the owner durability spine; recovery/checkpoint loss reproduces exact latest values; position-zero creation is digest-visible.\n- [ ] ADMIT: create or activate explicit dense-slot, SegmentEffect/kernel-checkpoint, owner/API, CLI, and application integration bones with dependency-correct ordering and production-shaped measurements.\n- [ ] DECLINE: bn-1lbf is closed as conditional work, dormant MetaStore checkpoint APIs are scheduled for removal/demotion, and the social sidecar remains explicitly discardable.\n- [ ] Both branches specify corruption, stale/ahead state, Process/Os/Group behavior, observability, and an adversarial review.\n\n# Project Value\nPrevents speculative state-kernel machinery for an unused API while preserving a clear path when a real engine-owned checkpoint consumer exists."}	blake3:cnkjpySIxqA6eWrQqY2jyQ1E-35Vmarxd9gdLNxnSOI
1784041995258804	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExogk		item.update	bn-1lbf	{"field":"title","value":"Add dense latest-value slots for admitted projection checkpoints"}	blake3:YOoo_1eEKDSy5cTZT74jkAyBDoby_xXXvNCpxp3S-d0
1784041995266843	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExowk		item.update	bn-1lbf	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nIf engine-owned projection checkpoints are admitted by bn-11mk, their latest values need dense resident cells with explicit presence/bottom semantics. Snapshot discovery no longer consumes these slots: its selected replacement is an immutable self-describing pack plus discardable manifest. This bone is conditional and must be closed without implementation if bn-11mk declines the product capability.\n\n# Goal\nFor the ADMIT branch only, add reusable dense latest-value projection-slot tables with explicit presence/bottom semantics, coherent publication, snapshot/export, and deterministic fold interfaces. Do not make them authoritative; canonical control and owner integration belongs to later admitted work.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] bn-11mk has an ADMIT decision and a concrete public checkpoint contract before implementation starts.\n- [ ] Cell format represents absent versus present-at-zero distinctly.\n- [ ] Batch/group apply and read snapshots are coherent with named publication frontiers.\n- [ ] Dirty tracking marks key creation even when the logical numeric value equals bottom.\n- [ ] Projector identifiers and optional digests have bounded validated encodings.\n- [ ] Loom/property tests cover torn pairs, growth, concurrent read, creation/update races, and checkpoint fallback.\n- [ ] Resident bytes, apply rate, and composed owner/recovery cost meet the decision bone's production-shaped budget.\n\n# Project Value\nSupplies the resident projection component only after the product earns it, avoiding speculative snapshot/checkpoint state."}	blake3:6OFrHZgef-6L5v_8-SqsIS5F-5WP4e696Q6ysBCXhTE
1784041995349797	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpAk		item.update	bn-1n7j	{"field":"title","value":"Phase 5: install dense heads and gate optional state capabilities"}	blake3:_gWB5Sp1_ONe_goiCf0AyQUYj6S_Pz705Psu4hdd3BI
1784041995353239	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpQk		item.update	bn-1n7j	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nSpike A admitted chunked dense stream-head pages with packed AtomicU128 cells and a seqlock fallback. Spike G admitted an exact epoch structure mechanically, but production dedupe is dormant and still needs the explicit product decision in bn-2ctq. The authority audit likewise found engine-owned projection checkpoints dormant, so bn-11mk must decide that capability before any dense projection slots are built.\n\n# Goal\nMove live stream heads into bounded direct pages owned by the flat owner, retire Book.heads after differential shadowing, and execute the independent product gates for engine-owned projection checkpoints and exact batch idempotency. Build their components only on an ADMIT branch; keep RegistryState canonical and strict.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Dense stream-head pages select lock-free packed cells by capability and use the verified seqlock fallback otherwise.\n- Head reads/publish/recovery shadow-compare against the old representation before cutover.\n- Book is reduced to registry/name concerns or replaced by explicit owner/read projections; no global head mutex remains.\n- Projection checkpoints receive a reviewed ADMIT/DECLINE before dense projection slots; DECLINE closes conditional work.\n- Exact dedupe semantics, scope, retention boundary, retry outcomes, collision exactness, and batch-level API are normative or explicitly declined before component work.\n- Any admitted active/frozen epoch or projection-slot implementation passes forced fault/collision and recovery/checkpoint-loss corpora.\n- Composed memory/latency gates are measured; synthetic component wins alone do not admit integration.\n\n# Exit Gate\nClose manually only after dense stream-head shadowing reports zero semantic divergence, the old head mutex/path is removed or explicitly retained with cause, both optional capabilities have reviewed decisions, every ADMIT branch has measured production components, every DECLINE branch is closed without dormant production code, and recovery/crash tests pass."}	blake3:Lvg81t-7AOjEWXCQ1l-2TSg47oj5HmNwbfswQlVxkSY
1784041995757296	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpgk		item.unlink	bn-11mk	{"target":"bn-1lbf"}	blake3:NAdYcuarJDBK5VGPcAAvMRXFa46nmh6pqL11ebuLgmk
1784041996173358	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpwk		item.unlink	bn-11mk	{"target":"bn-1mzi"}	blake3:SHv5vunAOPgKZ60SVh0kLUoyMSb5ZRHDrCSN2aD503I
