1784043108815340	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsgk		item.move	bn-25c	{"state":"done"}	blake3:IfZRJKZibFPV5bEbpmWi8pgNHbL4ghIJnY2c9uUsFC8
1784043347289458	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExswk		item.comment	bn-k8qd	{"body":"Adversarial review blocked cr-1fcqhq with nine amendments: dedupe boundary, Empty<Through(0), serialized writer/root/GC, build-vs-sealed pack state, bounded discovery scaling and durability modes, stable compatibility API, same-head repair, unverified-vs-certified threat boundary, and reproducible high-cardinality measurements. Amendments in progress."}	blake3:uT4SabzfSYlxPTUR2GobVo_6lPAxDN8aEp5cX1TIIw4
1784043533075603	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtAk		item.update	bn-ozi5	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nADR 0002 proves snapshots are discardable acceleration and freezes their replacement contract. The selected sidecar uses one exclusive writer, UUID-scoped non-reused identities, independently commit-framed build-pack records, immutable sealed packs, bounded copy-on-write discovery roots, and replay on every miss. No SnapshotInstalled log control is admitted.\n\n# Goal\nImplement the storage-neutral snapshot sidecar and the pre-1.0 public compatibility API without Fjall.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Add stable public SnapshotCompatibility and SnapshotCoverage values. Aggregate/schema and codec IDs are author-supplied canonical length-capped identifiers; type_name, TypeId, and unstable hashes are forbidden. Coverage total order is Empty < Through(0) < Through(1) and load is keyed by stream plus compatibility, or returns only strictly capped identity-bearing candidates.\n- [ ] Assign and implement the source-breaking Snapshottable/SnapshotStore trait work here, including aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, explicit compatibility lookup, and Buffered/Durable save selection.\n- [ ] Enforce one OS sidecar writer lock. All clones share a serialized writer owner; a second writer fails. Offline readers are read-only and never create, truncate, repair, rename, delete, or take the writer lock.\n- [ ] Persist one store UUID under the writer lock; PackId and root generations include that UUID and monotone non-reused sequences. Reserved temporary names are never candidates. Open selects the highest final independently resolvable valid root and falls back; only the writer truncates a torn active tail.\n- [ ] The active footerless build pack contains independently commit-framed bounded records. Root leaves bind exact PackId/offset/length/hash. Roll appends and syncs footer/index, seals/renames, syncs the directory, and never appends to a sealed pack. Cover concurrent pread versus append, crash at every roll step, and stale-FD/GC behavior.\n- [ ] Replace any flat O(all-heads) manifest with immutable content-addressed copy-on-write or equivalently bounded sharded discovery. Save groups update O(k log N) paths and publish a small self-contained root; lookup/open never enumerates all heads. Retain at least two complete roots.\n- [ ] Buffered is the default discardable-cache mode. Durable orders pack record before pages/root and syncs required files/directories before acknowledgement. Bounded clone-save grouping publishes one root, observes the strongest member mode, and reports group/barrier metrics.\n- [ ] Equal coverage validates current bytes first: invalid/unreadable may be repaired, identical valid is idempotent, and different valid is a conflict. Lower coverage cannot regress. Sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), corrupt-current repair, old/new compatibility, and lower/higher/equal tests pass.\n- [ ] UnverifiedCache omits both semantic hashes and documents the honest-writer assumption. CertifiedSnapshotRef requires and validates both state and prefix hashes. Exactly one hash is invalid; record hash is physical integrity and never a fold proof.\n- [ ] GC is writer-serialized: publish replacement/root, validate every retained root graph, prune obsolete roots, then delete only unreachable sealed pages/packs. Active pack is never collected; crashes leave only extra roots/orphans, never dangling retained roots.\n- [ ] Before candidate measurement, lock numeric budgets and run at least ten counterbalanced independent A/B pairs using run-level bootstrap, declared warmups/cache state, at least 10,000 operations for p99, host-load reject/retry, raw rows, and explicit durability normalization. Run 1/1K/100K/1M heads x 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states x low/medium/saturation save rates. Buffered compares to ordinary Fjall; Durable compares only to an explicitly synced/persisted Fjall control or prelocked absolute target. Grouped results are separate.\n- [ ] Warm resident lookup retains p50 <=50 ns/p99 <=150 ns. Snapshot-off same-host 32-cell before/after control uses the same methodology: Process >=95%, Group >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] No sidecar state authorizes event retention; corruption, unknown formats, or deletion always preserves canonical replay availability and public-path snapshot laws.\n\n# Project Value\nRemoves the only live Fjall role with bounded discovery scaling and explicit correctness, concurrency, trust, and durability contracts."}	blake3:TedgZHLwjfqFHOXGOxnqXyoSmvVB40-v8Qmlith6g0A
1784043550459110	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtQk		item.update	bn-3l8n	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nComponent replacement is insufficient: social, public exports/errors, doctor/inspect/retention, backup/restore, tests, goldens, and benchmarks encode Fjall snapshot behavior. ADR 0002 also introduces a stable source-breaking compatibility identity and explicit Buffered/Durable semantics that every caller must adopt.\n\n# Goal\nAdopt the bounded snapshot-pack/root replacement end to end across applications, public APIs, operational/offline tooling, backup policy, fixtures, observability, and product-path evidence before Fjall deletion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Migrate every Snapshottable implementation and SnapshotStore caller to stable aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, SnapshotCompatibility lookup, and SnapshotCoverage. No application, test, fixture, or tool derives identity from type_name, TypeId, or unstable hashes.\n- [ ] Social Store types, examples, benchmarks, public exports/errors/configuration, and feature flags use the replacement by default, expose Buffered/Durable policy intentionally, and instantiate no FjallSnapshotBackend.\n- [ ] Doctor and inspect open sidecars read-only, select only final independently resolvable roots, validate UUID/PackId/root/page/frame/trust identities, and report unverified, certified, invalid, repair/conflict, orphan, and fallback counts without repairing.\n- [ ] Retention and GC tools follow the writer-lock protocol and ordered retained-root reachability contract. Concurrent offline reads during append, pack roll, root publication, and GC return immutable correct bytes or miss/replay, never ABA.\n- [ ] Backup/restore policy explicitly includes or excludes discardable UUID-scoped packs/pages/roots; both branches test restored identity, stale files, missing store identity, and canonical replay fallback.\n- [ ] Golden fixtures are regenerated or receive a reviewed compatibility statement. Unknown sidecar formats miss safely; no stale meta-directory or flat-manifest assumption remains.\n- [ ] Public-path laws cover snapshot+tail equality, reopen/fold invalidation/subscription, sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), lower/higher/equal coverage, corrupt-current same-coverage repair, compatibility upgrades and late old-fold saves, second-writer rejection, clone serialization, torn records, every pack-roll/root/GC interruption, stale descriptors, and all semantic-hash presence modes.\n- [ ] Product-path measurement runs at least ten independent counterbalanced interleaved pairs with pair/run-level bootstrap, explicit warmups and cold/metadata-warm/resident cache state, at least 10,000 timed operations per p99 cell, predeclared host-load reject/retry, committed raw rows, and same-host same-session controls.\n- [ ] Exercise 1/1K/100K/1M discovery heads, 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states, and low/medium/saturation save rates. Record save/load/reopen p50/p99, root update bytes/pages, file count, write amplification, RSS, replayed events, group policy, and barrier counts. No operation linearly enumerates all heads.\n- [ ] Normalize durability: Buffered compares with ordinary Fjall; Durable compares only with a control that syncs blob/directories and persists Fjall, or a prelocked absolute target if exact equivalence is impossible. Report grouped durability separately and never headline-ratio unequal contracts.\n- [ ] Rerun the snapshot-off 32-cell control in the same host/session with the reproducible pair methodology: Process median >=95%, Group median >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, and no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] Adversarial review verifies application/offline-tool call graphs, bounded candidate discovery, backup behavior, and that Fjall removal is now mechanical. Sidecar failure never changes canonical event state or authorizes retention.\n\n# Project Value\nCloses the implementation-to-product gap with stable public identity, explicit durability, bounded million-head discovery, and operationally verified replay safety."}	blake3:pYpAgy9mqPrPSn1KsYKbMfWLF88HoOQRStbEqdYL__Y
1784043646002202	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtgk		item.comment	bn-3l8n	{"body":"Adoption acceptance amendment: fault injection must prove destructive GC ordering independently of snapshot save mode. A prune-directory barrier failure performs no dependent content deletion; after a durable prune, interrupted page/pack deletion may leave orphans but every surviving root resolves. Backup/restore and offline-reader tests must cover this Buffered-mode boundary."}	blake3:TP3u20-_KWUqkMr7_1su1ZeGlY4ad72DVBYeLzkhMEw
1784043646057274	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtwk		item.comment	bn-ozi5	{"body":"Acceptance amendment: destructive GC is a durability boundary independent of Buffered/Durable save mode. It must durably publish any replacement root, validate retained graphs, prune obsolete root descriptors and fsync the root directory before deleting any newly unreachable page/pack, then fsync every affected deletion directory. If the prune barrier fails, abort before content deletion; Buffered may defer reclamation but cannot weaken ordering."}	blake3:GXXtV6SsyyLtDC39XvQ9zwyNgmaYbzd0l0so3PrHSF4
1784043681038527	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuAk		item.update	bn-ozi5	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nADR 0002 proves snapshots are discardable acceleration and freezes their replacement contract. The selected sidecar uses one exclusive writer, UUID-scoped non-reused identities, independently commit-framed build-pack records, immutable sealed packs, bounded copy-on-write discovery roots, and replay on every miss. No SnapshotInstalled log control is admitted.\n\n# Goal\nImplement the storage-neutral snapshot sidecar and the pre-1.0 public compatibility API without Fjall.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Add stable public SnapshotCompatibility and SnapshotCoverage values. Aggregate/schema and codec IDs are author-supplied canonical length-capped identifiers; type_name, TypeId, and unstable hashes are forbidden. Coverage total order is Empty < Through(0) < Through(1) and load is keyed by stream plus compatibility, or returns only strictly capped identity-bearing candidates.\n- [ ] Assign and implement the source-breaking Snapshottable/SnapshotStore trait work here, including aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, explicit compatibility lookup, and Buffered/Durable save selection.\n- [ ] Enforce one OS sidecar writer lock. All clones share a serialized writer owner; a second writer fails. Offline readers are read-only and never create, truncate, repair, rename, delete, or take the writer lock.\n- [ ] Persist one store UUID under the writer lock; PackId and root generations include that UUID and monotone non-reused sequences. Reserved temporary names are never candidates. Open selects the highest final independently resolvable valid root and falls back; only the writer truncates a torn active tail.\n- [ ] The active footerless build pack contains independently commit-framed bounded records. Root leaves bind exact PackId/offset/length/hash. Roll appends and syncs footer/index, seals/renames, syncs the directory, and never appends to a sealed pack. Cover concurrent pread versus append, crash at every roll step, and stale-FD/GC behavior.\n- [ ] Replace any flat O(all-heads) manifest with immutable content-addressed copy-on-write or equivalently bounded sharded discovery. Save groups update O(k log N) paths and publish a small self-contained root; lookup/open never enumerates all heads. Retain at least two complete roots.\n- [ ] Buffered is the default discardable-cache mode. Durable orders pack record before pages/root and syncs required files/directories before acknowledgement. Bounded clone-save grouping publishes one root, observes the strongest member mode, and reports group/barrier metrics.\n- [ ] Equal coverage validates current bytes first: invalid/unreadable may be repaired, identical valid is idempotent, and different valid is a conflict. Lower coverage cannot regress. Sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), corrupt-current repair, old/new compatibility, and lower/higher/equal tests pass.\n- [ ] UnverifiedCache omits both semantic hashes and documents the honest-writer assumption. CertifiedSnapshotRef requires and validates both state and prefix hashes. Exactly one hash is invalid; record hash is physical integrity and never a fold proof.\n- [ ] GC is writer-serialized and destructive GC is a durability boundary independent of save mode: durably publish any replacement root, validate every retained graph, prune obsolete root descriptors and fsync the root directory before deleting any newly unreachable page/pack, then fsync every affected deletion directory. A failed prune barrier aborts before content deletion; Buffered may defer reclamation but cannot weaken ordering. The active pack is never collected; crashes leave only extra roots/orphans, never a dangling surviving root.\n- [ ] Before candidate measurement, lock numeric budgets and run at least ten counterbalanced independent A/B pairs using run-level bootstrap, declared warmups/cache state, at least 10,000 operations for p99, host-load reject/retry, raw rows, and explicit durability normalization. Run 1/1K/100K/1M heads x 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states x low/medium/saturation save rates. Buffered compares to ordinary Fjall; Durable compares only to an explicitly synced/persisted Fjall control or prelocked absolute target. Grouped results are separate.\n- [ ] Warm resident lookup retains p50 <=50 ns/p99 <=150 ns. Snapshot-off same-host 32-cell before/after control uses the same methodology: Process >=95%, Group >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] No sidecar state authorizes event retention; corruption, unknown formats, or deletion always preserves canonical replay availability and public-path snapshot laws.\n\n# Project Value\nRemoves the only live Fjall role with bounded discovery scaling and explicit correctness, concurrency, trust, and durability contracts."}	blake3:D7BQB_-SArl3MzBUrD5P4GgTQCWjPK5Noy3_aqF9eys
1784043689123448	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuQk		item.update	bn-3l8n	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nComponent replacement is insufficient: social, public exports/errors, doctor/inspect/retention, backup/restore, tests, goldens, and benchmarks encode Fjall snapshot behavior. ADR 0002 also introduces a stable source-breaking compatibility identity and explicit Buffered/Durable semantics that every caller must adopt.\n\n# Goal\nAdopt the bounded snapshot-pack/root replacement end to end across applications, public APIs, operational/offline tooling, backup policy, fixtures, observability, and product-path evidence before Fjall deletion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Migrate every Snapshottable implementation and SnapshotStore caller to stable aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, SnapshotCompatibility lookup, and SnapshotCoverage. No application, test, fixture, or tool derives identity from type_name, TypeId, or unstable hashes.\n- [ ] Social Store types, examples, benchmarks, public exports/errors/configuration, and feature flags use the replacement by default, expose Buffered/Durable policy intentionally, and instantiate no FjallSnapshotBackend.\n- [ ] Doctor and inspect open sidecars read-only, select only final independently resolvable roots, validate UUID/PackId/root/page/frame/trust identities, and report unverified, certified, invalid, repair/conflict, orphan, and fallback counts without repairing.\n- [ ] Retention and GC tools follow the writer lock and make destructive GC durable independent of save mode: durably publish replacements, validate retained graphs, fsync obsolete-root pruning before dependent content deletion, then fsync deletion directories. A prune-barrier failure deletes no newly unreachable content. Concurrent offline reads during append, pack roll, root publication, and GC return immutable correct bytes or miss/replay, never ABA.\n- [ ] Backup/restore policy explicitly includes or excludes discardable UUID-scoped packs/pages/roots; both branches test restored identity, stale files, missing store identity, and canonical replay fallback.\n- [ ] Golden fixtures are regenerated or receive a reviewed compatibility statement. Unknown sidecar formats miss safely; no stale meta-directory or flat-manifest assumption remains.\n- [ ] Public-path laws cover snapshot+tail equality, reopen/fold invalidation/subscription, sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), lower/higher/equal coverage, corrupt-current same-coverage repair, compatibility upgrades and late old-fold saves, second-writer rejection, clone serialization, torn records, every pack-roll/root/GC interruption, stale descriptors, and all semantic-hash presence modes.\n- [ ] Product-path measurement runs at least ten independent counterbalanced interleaved pairs with pair/run-level bootstrap, explicit warmups and cold/metadata-warm/resident cache state, at least 10,000 timed operations per p99 cell, predeclared host-load reject/retry, committed raw rows, and same-host same-session controls.\n- [ ] Exercise 1/1K/100K/1M discovery heads, 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states, and low/medium/saturation save rates. Record save/load/reopen p50/p99, root update bytes/pages, file count, write amplification, RSS, replayed events, group policy, and barrier counts. No operation linearly enumerates all heads.\n- [ ] Normalize durability: Buffered compares with ordinary Fjall; Durable compares only with a control that syncs blob/directories and persists Fjall, or a prelocked absolute target if exact equivalence is impossible. Report grouped durability separately and never headline-ratio unequal contracts.\n- [ ] Rerun the snapshot-off 32-cell control in the same host/session with the reproducible pair methodology: Process median >=95%, Group median >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, and no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] Adversarial review verifies application/offline-tool call graphs, bounded candidate discovery, backup behavior, and that Fjall removal is now mechanical. Sidecar failure never changes canonical event state or authorizes retention.\n\n# Project Value\nCloses the implementation-to-product gap with stable public identity, explicit durability, bounded million-head discovery, and operationally verified replay safety."}	blake3:riiL2vFoP9Cv5ivys2UhHwusxKTrB1h0ezkNZRgjcEg
1784044242580000	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExugk		item.comment	bn-k8qd	{"body":"Applied the nine cr-1fcqhq amendments plus lead follow-up: inclusive dedupe boundary; Empty<Through(0); stable compatibility API; single-writer/anti-ABA lifecycle; footerless commit-framed build packs and seal recovery; bounded COW discovery; explicit Buffered/Durable/grouped publication; equal-coverage corrupt-head repair; semantic trust boundary; reproducible high-cardinality A/B; and destructive GC fsync ordering independent of save mode. Updated bn-ozi5 and bn-3l8n acceptance descriptions. Checks: diff clean, fmt-check pass; initial full suite 949/950 pass before interrupting documented 3000-iteration (~62 min) snapshot law at 476.9s; bounded 25-iteration snapshot suite 4/4 pass; transient fold-chain envelope failure under loaded rerun passed isolated."}	blake3:w3HwyfzqYGHOl1asMfVu-l_gC6pDuWth7T4Ap7adbM0
1784044852147473	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuwk		item.update	bn-ozi5	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nADR 0002 proves snapshots are discardable acceleration and freezes their replacement contract. The selected sidecar uses one exclusive writer, UUID-scoped non-reused identities, independently commit-framed build-pack records, immutable sealed packs, bounded copy-on-write discovery roots, and replay on every miss. No SnapshotInstalled log control is admitted.\n\n# Goal\nImplement the storage-neutral snapshot sidecar and the pre-1.0 public compatibility API without Fjall.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Add stable public SnapshotCompatibility and SnapshotCoverage values. Aggregate/schema and codec IDs are author-supplied canonical length-capped identifiers; type_name, TypeId, and unstable hashes are forbidden. Coverage total order is Empty < Through(0) < Through(1) and load is keyed by stream plus compatibility, or returns only strictly capped identity-bearing candidates.\n- [ ] Assign and implement the source-breaking Snapshottable/SnapshotStore trait work here, including aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, explicit compatibility lookup, and Buffered/Durable save selection.\n- [ ] Enforce one OS sidecar writer lock. All clones share a serialized writer owner; a second writer fails. Offline readers are read-only and never create, truncate, repair, rename, delete, or take the writer lock.\n- [ ] Persist one store UUID under the writer lock; PackId and root generations include that UUID and monotone non-reused sequences. Reserved temporary names are never candidates. Open selects the highest final independently resolvable valid root and falls back; only the writer truncates a torn active tail.\n- [ ] The active footerless build pack contains independently commit-framed bounded records. Root leaves bind exact PackId/offset/length/hash. Roll appends and syncs footer/index, seals/renames, syncs the directory, and never appends to a sealed pack. Cover concurrent pread versus append, crash at every roll step, and stale-FD/GC behavior.\n- [ ] Replace any flat O(all-heads) manifest with immutable content-addressed copy-on-write or equivalently bounded sharded discovery. Save groups update O(k log N) paths and publish a small self-contained root; ordinary lookup/open never enumerates all heads. Implement pinned-root bounded-memory scan_snapshots(cursor, limit): root-bound capped opaque cursors, shared deletion lease, O(log N + limit) work, O(height + limit) memory, partial diagnostics, and fail-closed destructive traversal. Retain at least two complete roots.\n- [ ] Buffered is the default discardable-cache mode. Durable means complete-root survival: before acknowledgement, promote and sync every reachable pack frontier/page and creation/rename directory entry not proven by a prior acknowledged Durable root or synced proof ledger, including unrelated Buffered-only state, existing content-addressed pages whose write was skipped, and a new active .open pack directory entry. Bounded clone-save grouping observes the strongest member mode and reports promotion bytes/files/pages/frontiers plus data/directory/ledger/root barriers. Inject every promotion/sync failure and forbid acknowledgement.\n- [ ] Equal coverage validates current bytes first: invalid/unreadable may be repaired, identical valid is idempotent, and different valid is a conflict. Lower coverage cannot regress. Sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), corrupt-current repair, old/new compatibility, and lower/higher/equal tests pass.\n- [ ] UnverifiedCache omits both semantic hashes and documents the honest-writer assumption. CertifiedSnapshotRef requires and validates both state and prefix hashes. Exactly one hash is invalid; record hash is physical integrity and never a fold proof.\n- [ ] GC is writer-serialized and destructive GC is a durability boundary independent of save mode. Readability is insufficient: first promote the complete closure and acknowledge a new Durable root, then validate additional retained graphs, prune obsolete roots and fsync the root directory, delete only unreachable content, and fsync deletion directories. Promotion/root failure prevents pruning; prune failure prevents deletion. Buffered may defer reclamation but cannot weaken ordering. Test GC re-root reuse and every sync failure; the active pack is never collected.\n- [ ] Before candidate measurement, lock numeric budgets and run at least ten counterbalanced independent A/B pairs using run-level bootstrap, declared warmups/cache state, at least 10,000 operations for p99, host-load reject/retry, raw rows, and explicit durability normalization. Run 1/1K/100K/1M heads x 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states x low/medium/saturation save rates plus a one-million-head full administrative scan with wall/RSS results. Buffered compares to ordinary Fjall; Durable compares only to an explicitly synced/persisted Fjall control or prelocked absolute target. Report closure-promotion bytes/files/pages/frontiers and data/directory/ledger/root barriers; grouped results are separate.\n- [ ] Warm resident lookup retains p50 <=50 ns/p99 <=150 ns. Snapshot-off same-host 32-cell before/after control uses the same methodology: Process >=95%, Group >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] No sidecar state authorizes event retention; corruption, unknown formats, or deletion always preserves canonical replay availability and public-path snapshot laws.\n\n# Project Value\nRemoves the only live Fjall role with bounded discovery scaling and explicit correctness, concurrency, trust, and durability contracts."}	blake3:7ytsCUDZvTIS9j7kZjx9znm3xnqfPji7dObkg3Xx8Po
1784044876824706	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvAk		item.update	bn-3l8n	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nComponent replacement is insufficient: social, public exports/errors, doctor/inspect/retention, backup/restore, tests, goldens, and benchmarks encode Fjall snapshot behavior. ADR 0002 also introduces a stable source-breaking compatibility identity and explicit Buffered/Durable semantics that every caller must adopt.\n\n# Goal\nAdopt the bounded snapshot-pack/root replacement end to end across applications, public APIs, operational/offline tooling, backup policy, fixtures, observability, and product-path evidence before Fjall deletion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Migrate every Snapshottable implementation and SnapshotStore caller to stable aggregate/schema ID, fold version, codec ID/version, SnapshotCompatibility lookup, and SnapshotCoverage. No application, test, fixture, or tool derives identity from type_name, TypeId, or unstable hashes.\n- [ ] Social Store types, examples, benchmarks, public exports/errors/configuration, and feature flags use the replacement by default, expose Buffered/Durable policy intentionally, and instantiate no FjallSnapshotBackend.\n- [ ] Doctor and inspect open sidecars read-only, select one final independently resolvable pinned root, and enumerate through capped root-bound scan_snapshots cursors with O(height + limit) memory. They validate UUID/PackId/root/page/frame/trust identities and report unverified, certified, invalid, repair/conflict, orphan, fallback, and explicit partial/corrupt scan counts without repairing.\n- [ ] Retention and GC tools follow the writer lock and make destructive GC durable independent of save mode. GC first promotes a complete closure and acknowledges a Durable root; readability alone is insufficient. It then validates retained graphs, fsyncs obsolete-root pruning before deletion, and fsyncs deletion directories. Retention completes a corruption-free pinned-root scan and revalidates the same root before mutation; partial/corrupt traversal fails closed. Concurrent offline reads return immutable correct bytes or miss/replay, never ABA.\n- [ ] Backup/restore policy explicitly includes or excludes discardable UUID-scoped packs/pages/roots; both branches test restored identity, stale files, missing store identity, and canonical replay fallback.\n- [ ] Golden fixtures are regenerated or receive a reviewed compatibility statement. Unknown sidecar formats miss safely; no stale meta-directory or flat-manifest assumption remains.\n- [ ] Public-path laws cover snapshot+tail equality, reopen/fold invalidation/subscription, sequential and concurrent Empty/Through(0), lower/higher/equal coverage, corrupt-current repair, compatibility upgrades, writer/clone serialization, torn records, pack-roll/root/GC interruption, stale descriptors, and trust modes. Durable crash cases include Buffered A content reused by different-key Durable B, skipped existing-page writes, lost .open directory entry, GC re-root reuse, and every promotion/data/directory/ledger/root sync failure; failures cannot acknowledge or authorize deletion. Admin cases cover root-mismatched cursors, pin/GC races, corrupt middle pages, partial diagnostics, and fail-closed retention.\n- [ ] Product-path measurement runs at least ten independent counterbalanced interleaved pairs with pair/run-level bootstrap, explicit warmups and cold/metadata-warm/resident cache state, at least 10,000 timed operations per p99 cell, predeclared host-load reject/retry, committed raw rows, and same-host same-session controls.\n- [ ] Exercise 1/1K/100K/1M discovery heads, 64 B/4 KiB/1 MiB states, and low/medium/saturation save rates. Ordinary open/point lookup never enumerates all heads. Separately run a complete paginated one-million-head administrative scan and record wall time, pages/entries, peak RSS, and partial/corrupt behavior. Record save/load/reopen p50/p99, root update bytes/pages, file count, write amplification, RSS, replayed events, group policy, and barrier counts.\n- [ ] Normalize durability: Buffered compares with ordinary Fjall; complete-closure Durable compares only with a control that syncs blob/directories and persists Fjall, or a prelocked absolute target if exact equivalence is impossible. Report closure-promotion bytes/files/pages/pack frontiers, creation/rename directory barriers, ledger/root barriers, and proven no-I/O reuse. Report grouped durability separately and never headline-ratio unequal contracts.\n- [ ] Rerun the snapshot-off 32-cell control in the same host/session with the reproducible pair methodology: Process median >=95%, Group median >=90%, p99 regression <=10%, and no added barriers/syscalls.\n- [ ] Adversarial review verifies application/offline-tool call graphs, bounded candidate discovery, backup behavior, and that Fjall removal is now mechanical. Sidecar failure never changes canonical event state or authorizes retention.\n\n# Project Value\nCloses the implementation-to-product gap with stable public identity, explicit durability, bounded million-head discovery, and operationally verified replay safety."}	blake3:wgCXlq9S7mICH2IsPNfNWL41GrPfRaAh9lyP3X02rAk
1784045085624981	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvQk		item.comment	bn-k8qd	{"body":"Final re-review blockers amended: Durable now means complete-root survival with explicit proof-ledger/prior-Durable reuse, promotion of all inherited Buffered content and file/directory closure, and GC anchored by a complete-closure Durable root before prune/delete. Added pinned-root capped paginated scan_snapshots for admin enumeration, bounded memory, partial diagnostics, fail-closed retention, and 1M full-scan evidence. Mirrored in design, R5/R9/R10, bn-ozi5, bn-3l8n, and cr-1fcqhq reply th-19zpx9.2. Checks: diff clean, fmt-check pass, bounded-law full suite 950/950 pass in 133.319s (26 skipped)."}	blake3:UF7akbfsoS0jT4fxEtldHvzZ_JbDrZU15P-1f-Q_R88
