1784063994196396	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx_gk		item.create	bn-1gn1	{"description":"Context: bn-3eg0 proved that coupling a 256 MiB preparation cap to global strict FIFO/readiness scheduling causes unacceptable tiny-tail regressions (13.58x in the isolated-core causal study). The memory-safety concern remains separable from scheduling. Goal: bound engine-owned prepared construction memory while preserving the current production admission/order behavior and same-stream winner semantics. Acceptance: (1) no new priority queue, size-class reordering, or cross-class winner changes; (2) explicit conservative build-peak accounting including PreparedBatch internal vectors, names/slots/subframes/hash scratch; (3) cancellation/close releases exact permits and no unbounded metadata queue; (4) public-path owned and borrowed submissions both covered; (5) paired Process/Group batches 1/10/100/1000 and mixed large+tiny show throughput >=95%, p99 <=110%, barrier parity, and bounded high-water; (6) otherwise record DECLINED with production unchanged. Dependency: integrate after owned append so the deployed path, not borrowed-only scaffolding, is measured.","kind":"task","labels":["asterism","engine","memory","roadmap","risk:high"],"parent":"bn-3ef","size":"m","title":"Bound prepared construction memory without priority scheduling"}	blake3:H63vscO9fMqgeIPYglivMyr3gJiMr0NaC6WRVZZj2Ss
