1784131397628389	mess-publication-v2	itc:v3:AWLJJn5JyTJM_QAAAAAAQdVv1dWrfgAAAAEvCQ		item.comment	bn-5mc9	{"body":"Candidate-only diagnosis complete. Temporary env-gated sidecar checkpoint 1da7b53; 30 rows (10 each Process/b1, Process/b100, Group/b1000) retained with provenance/hashes/results under spikes/publication_v2 in restoration commit 5491291. Group/b1000: 10 sampled commit groups, sampled width mean 3.9/max 4, 9 inflight-drained + 1 deadline; mean phases direct 3293.276us, post-I/O-to-frontier 1.692us, frontier-to-first 0.944us, first-to-last 4.782us. This establishes Group/b1000 fsync domination only; Process/b1 still has about 3.279us after frontier vs 5.763us direct and needs paired admission to judge. Locked harness restored via apply_patch to SHA-256 e063a95a1df126e9e81ec7a336ce177f1d8dab0af66aaaaa086f546273367a21. Diagnosis-only production OwnerDiagnostics/API/sampler/tests removed separately in f2f3a1b; canonical frontier/post-cut architecture preserved. Fmt/check green; append-gate debug 12/12 and release 12/12. Clean final HEAD f2f3a1bdd7f887ea2c020042dfcd9e10b4537742 release benchmark SHA-256 148417566bdc8984e41a3e628313e3bac9d3372c93ab96c566855c9cb2c7007a. No paired ABBA/merge/close/release."}	blake3:6ZdwtF7SnP5cJXYYAVu0AlCVHerOFIrOlP3fpdfN99g
1784132299381043	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkAo		item.create	bn-2c91	{"description":"# Context & evidence\nThe standalone grouped-publication candidates bn-3vj4 and bn-5mc9 proved the one-authoritative-frontier contract correct but failed locked production gates. The diagnostics-free v2 candidate improved Process/b1 from 0.934063x to 0.962144x control yet remained below 0.97; Group/b1000 issued 1015 barriers versus 1008 control. Adding the cut atop Book plus the current ActiveIndex does not pay for itself.\n\n# Goal\nAfter dense heads and active stream microblocks are integrated, make one landed DirectCommitter group the native publication unit across RegistryState, dense heads, stream microblocks, stride-1 global pointers, the canonical read frontier, and ordered completions. Reuse the bn-5mc9 correctness proof while removing the legacy locks/index passes that caused the standalone fixed-cost regression.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n- Consume the full landed group once in canonical global order; registry-only, partial ordered-unit, independent-unit, poison, cancellation, Exact/Os, roll, and reopen semantics match the retained bn-5mc9 corpus.\n- Stage dense-head, microblock, and stride-1 global effects while hidden, then release exactly one authoritative frontier before ordered cache warm/completion; readers observe the pre-group state or a complete published prefix.\n- Production apply uses dense-head page batches and microblock-native insertion, not a compatibility Book/ActiveIndex staging layer; Book.heads and the old stream map cannot be reintroduced.\n- Loom models concurrent frontier advancers and microblock publication/reclamation; deterministic seams cover post-stage/pre-release and post-release/pre-completion reads.\n- Rerun the locked Process/b1, Process/b100, and Group/b1000 ABBA screen with throughput >=0.97, p99 <=1.10, allocations/bytes <=1.05, Group aggregate barriers <=100.25%, and median barrier delta <=0 before the Phase 6 composed matrix.\n- If the focused gate misses, retain per-plan publication on the new representations and remove the one-cut branch; no dormant selector remains.\n\n# Integration boundary\nThis task starts only after dense-head cutover, microblock stream-read integration, and publication/reclamation safety are green. It blocks the final production microblock gate, so the decision is made on the composed engine rather than another isolated spike.","kind":"task","labels":["asterism","engine","microblocks","state-kernel","risk:high","roadmap"],"parent":"bn-34as","size":"m","title":"Compose canonical group publication with dense heads and microblocks"}	blake3:JC1AW6pGXnvE0ixh0bSHco254lcwSYp0pMCpTlyT_4c
